resses when the receiver holds a different address (words of engine.cljc:1388-1393 `:dependency-pin-mismatch`). The lower stays pure over the receiver value and attaches nothing on refusal (attach-count law); the receiver's registry is still kept as given. (3) R4: carried `:install` children: the lower refuses a child unless its manifest address is in a composition-supplied opts set `{:yin.k/admitted {name address}}` (default empty = fail closed), as `:yin.k/unsatisfied {:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {name carried-address}}}` before any attach (section 4.4); and at `link-install` (engine.cljc ~:1436-1443) the copied sender `:admission` record must not stand for the receiver's decision: replace it by the receiver's (opts-supplied) record or drop it, as the report specifies. (4) Documentation: continuation 2.5 and 7.2 (the lower now re-discharges registry names by pinned address; Q5 answered C), UCF 7.11, the refusal shape, and the FORBIDDEN list for a composition's fetch loop (section 4.2 last bullet, section 5) in the right design doc; update docs/agents/known-gaps.md rows (Q5, R4 install-child admission). The fetch LOOP itself is NOT part of this slice (composition policy; no fetch code in the VM or lower; do not add one). TESTS (portable .cljc, section 7.1): pin equal-address satisfaction, different-address refusal naming both addresses, missing-module refusal before attach with attach-count zero, host-module nil pin with equal and unequal profiles, install child refused with empty admitted set and accepted when listed, `link-install` no longer copies the sender's admission, the decoded pack round-trips the new slot, malformed slot refused (add to malformed_rows UCF collection like the :equality-collapse entry), and a mutant for each (name-only satisfaction regress: test fails). RULES: no src/yang, no test/yang, no collab commits, no `--yolo`; if any pinned A address, descriptor hash or golden other than rows fixtures carrying requires/install moves, STOP and rep