e/layout, Stage E, linker,\\n  linker-manifest, mint and `^dao\\\\.jing\\\\..*`. Log:\\n  `/tmp/module-pins-independent-focused-unrestricted.log`.\\n- Kondo on all four changed Clojure files: **0 errors, 0 warnings**.\\n- `git diff --check`: clean.\\n- Whole unrestricted JVM quick tier (`clojure -M:test -e :slow`):\\n  **4025 tests, 249902 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors**, exit 0. Log:\\n  `/tmp/module-pins-independent-quick-unrestricted.log`.\\n\\n## Proposed split after completion\\n\\n1. Carrier/lift/lower code; tests plus fixture re-mint must accompany it to\\n   produce a coherent passing commit. Docs complete I-8 with old/new addresses.\\n2. Driver seam and regression are separable from the carrier; this partial work\\n   verifies that seam against commit 1's existing admission gate.\\n3. Documentation may be reviewed separately, but must describe actual code and\\n   fixture state at landing. No staging or commit performed here.\\n\\nNo `src/yang` or `test/yang` edits. No pinned A address, descriptor hash or golden\\nchanged. Existing untracked collab files preserved. No collab commits.\\n\\nBLOCKED\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/1793600000000-engineer-module-pins-r2c.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:14:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1793550000000-architect-module-pins-review.report.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-16 06:06:47 GMT\\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-16 13:06:47 +07\\nCoding-Agent: claude (claude-fable-5-1)\\nSession-ID: pending\\nRole: Architect (read-only; worktree datomworld-srvm-pins, branch srvm-module-pins @ 6df441d0, 13 uncommitted files)\\nBrief: collab/1793540000000-architect-module-pins-review.prompt.md\\nInputs: collab/1792130530811-engineer-module-pins.report.md, collab/1793520000000-architect-fetch-threat-model.report.md (§4.2, §4.4, §6), the full `git diff`, and the sources cited below.\\n\\n# Module pins: Part A review of R4, Part B ruling on host-module pins, Part C round-2 steps\\n\\n## Part A: review of the uncommitted R4 part\\n\\n### A.0 What was checked\\n\\n- Gate placement: `check-install-admission!` (`rows.cljc:1883-1892`) runs in `lower-task` after `check-custody!` and before `attach-streams!` (`rows.cljc:2301-2304`), over every task of `task-tree` (`rows.cljc:1805-1808`, root and every nested install child, pre-order). Refusal throws before the first attach: the attach-count law holds (tests assert zero attaches).\\n- Paths that lower install children: only `rows/lower-task`. Backends (`layout/lower-task`) refuse `:installs` already; `remote.cljc:485` lowers no installs; fork packs go through the same `lower-task`; `holder.export/rehydrate-fenced` now forwards `:yin.k/admitted` (`export.cljc:539`); the holder driver's two lower paths are discussed in P2-1.\\n- Other copies of the sender's admission: `engine/link-install` (`engine.cljc:1436-1443`) is the only consumer of the four `:yin.admit/*` response fields outside the linker; nothing else reads the installed entry's `:admission` (grep over `src`: only `linker/admission.cljc`, `linker/interpreter.cljc`, `yin.repl` configuration, none read `(:admission entry)`). Dropping rather than replacing is safe for consumers.\\n- Refusal shape: `{:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied :yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {name carried-address}}}` matches threat-model §4.4 exactly (no `:yin.k/kind`, no `:yin.k/discovery`). The carried address can never be nil at this point because `check-install!` already required a manifest map (`rows.cljc:1846-1851`), so `{'host.mod nil}` in the admitted map correctly refuses.\\n- Mutants: all three are meaningful (name-only acceptance, retained sender admission, gate bypass) and each is killed by distinct assertions. Mutant 2 has to be re-done after P1-1 (see below).\\n- Tests: portable (plain data, keyword sentinel addresses, host-neutral catch forms, kondo clean per the engineer). Fixtures admit their fixed manifests explicitly from the composition side (`rows_support.cljc:298-301`, `safepoint_harness_test.cljc:349-352`), never derived from the pack.\\n- Docs: continuation §2.5 and §7.1 (\\\"the lower does not re-discharge free names\\\") are unchanged and still true, since the pin work has not landed. UCF §7.6.4/§7.6.5 are unchanged spec text. The §7.11 row, continuation Q5, revisions I-8 and the known-gaps rows say \\\"blocked\\\" for the pin carrier: no overclaim. The claims that are wrong after P1-1 are listed under P3-3.\\n\\n### A.1 Findings\\n\\n**P1-1. Dropping the sender's admission at restore breaks fenced recovery and the relift law for every real pack with an install child.**\\nThe lift copies the install record's `response` whole into the `:install` row (`install-node`, `rows.cljc:1643`). The linker's interpreter puts `:yin.admit/id`, `:yin.admit/decision`, `:yin.admit/asserters` and `:yin.admit/address` on every successful DHT-admitted response (`interpreter.cljc:416-421`), so a real pack's `:install` row carries them. The new restore-side `dissoc` (`rows.cljc:2236-2237`) then produces a machine whose `:installs` response lacks the four keys. Consequences:\\n- `rehydrate-fenced` re-prepares and re-encodes the restored machine and demands byte equality with the published pack (`export.cljc:548-556`); the relift's install row now differs from the carried one, so every fenced recovery of such a pack answers `:yin.k/undecodable :recovery-inconsistent`.\\n- The harness law \\\"the relift equals the lift by root\\\" (`safepoint_harness_test.cljc:10`, asserted at `:629` via `canonical-under`) fails for the same packs.\\nThe current tests pass only because every fixture response (`rows_support/module-response`, `blocking-body`) carries no `:yin.admit/*` keys. This is a correctness defect, not a test gap.\\nRequired fix (revert-not-fix does not apply, this is the slice's own line): strip the four `:yin.admit/*` keys **at lift**, in `install-node`, so the pack never carries S's decision (\\\"the carrier narrows, never widens\\\", §4.1), and make the lower **refuse** a carried response that still carries any `:yin.admit/*` key as `:yin.k/undecodable :install-response` (one clause in `check-install!`'s existing `and`; hand-crafted packs only). Delete the restore-side `dissoc`. Then the restored response equals the carried one, fenced reproduction and the relift law hold by construction, and `link-install` sees no sender record. New pin for the mutant: a source whose install response carries the record lifts to an `:install` row without the keys (assert on the decoded row's slot 3), and a pack with the keys spliced back in is refused before attach with zero attaches. Keep the existing \\\"installed entry has no `:admission`\\\" assertion.\\n\\n**P2-1. The holder driver has no seam to supply `:yin.k/admitted`, so the composition's real lower path refuses every pack with an install child.**\\n`driver/lowered` is called with `{:exclusive true}` (`driver.cljc:2294`) and with the grant map (`driver.cljc:1588-1600`); the fenced recovery at `driver.cljc:2455-2457` passes only `:address` and `:attach`. None forwards an admitted map. This is fail-closed (safe) but it means R4 as written makes carried install children unreachable through the holder, with no driver test noticing (`driver_test.cljc` has no install-child handoff; `:2726` fakes one for gate-mode only). Required for round 2, not for landing R4 alone: a config entry `(:yin.k/admitted-modules (:config state))` forwarded by `lowered` and by the fenced recovery call (two lines), plus one driver test that lowers a parked-installer checkpoint with and without the config. Until then, a known-gaps row \\\"holder driver passes no admitted-modules map; install-child handoff through the driver refuses\\\" (P2) must land with R4.\\n\\n**P2-2. `:yin.k/admitted` already means two other things in the same vocabulary.**\\nIt is a ledger fact kind, \\\"one effect's dedup record with its result\\\" (`ledger.cljc:22, 115, 553`), and the driver's not-holder answer field for the admitted variant set (`driver.cljc:743, 1655`). The threat model (§4.4, my text) chose the word carelessly. Rename the lower option to `:yin.k/admitted-modules` in `rows.cljc`, `export.cljc`, the five test files and the five doc amendments. Cheap now, a permanent vocabulary defect after commit.\\n\\n**P3-1. The gate reports one child, not the complete set, and omits `:yin.k/discovery`.**\\nEvery other `:yin.k/unsatisfied` from the lower carries `:yin.k/discovery` (`rows.cljc:1629, 1686, 1923, 1930`). §4.4's shape omitted it; §4.2's has `:complete`. Ruling: in round 2 fold the admission gate into the single `check-modules!` stage (Part C step 5), which collects every unlisted child of the tree and every unsatisfied pin into one `:yin.k/missing` map with `:yin.k/discovery :complete`. Not blocking for landing R4 alone; the §4.4 shape is acceptable until then.\\n\\n**P3-2. Name-keyed admission across the tree.** The admitted map is flat by module name over the whole tree. A nested child that installs the same name as a sibling at another address cannot be admitted. The registry family makes this a degenerate case; note it in the `lower-task` docstring, no code.\\n\\n**P3-3. Doc statements to retarget after P1-1.** Continuation §7.2 amendment (\\\"Restore drops the sender's …\\\"), Q3 amendment (\\\"drops the sender's admission evidence on restore\\\"), `yin.vm.linker.dht.md:2333-2335`, transport-tuples amendment (\\\"Restore drops the sender's four …\\\"), revisions I-8 (\\\"restore drops\\\"), known-gaps R4 row (\\\"sender admission dropped on restore\\\"). All become \\\"the lift never carries the sender's admission fields; a carried one is `:yin.k/undecodable :install-response`\\\". Also replace `:yin.k/admitted` by the P2-2 name in all five docs.\\n\\n**P3-4. `holder.export/rehydrate-fenced` docstring** says \\\"default empty\\\" twice in different words; fine. No change needed.\\n\\nVerdict for Part A: **CHANGES-REQUIRED** (P1-1 blocking; P2-2 rename and the P2-1 ledger row land with it; P3-1/P3-2 deferred to round 2).\\n\\n## Part B: ruling on host-module (\\\"nil\\\") pins\\n\\n### B.0 Facts the ruling rests on\\n\\n- A host-registered entry has `:address nil` and lists its exports as `:yin.module/primitives {sym profile-address}` (`register-host-module`, `module.cljc:223-263`). `module/host-export-profile` answers exactly that profile address for a qualified symbol (`module.cljc:266-281`): a **keyword** `:yin.k.pp/blake3-…` minted by `vm/primitive-profile` over `{name class arities effects host-state}` (`vm.cljc:338-356`). Plain data, no functions, no host objects. The core `stream` and `cell` modules are host modules with literal cljc profiles and `:none` host-state (`module.cljc:350-363, 405-410`), so their addresses are identical on JVM, Node and Dart.\\n- The linker already defines \\\"satisfied by equal profile\\\" for exactly this case: `declared-discharge` discharges a primitive obligation by `(= profile (module/host-export-profile modules name))` (`linker.cljc:1014-1018`), and a module obligation by equal manifest address (`:1022-1027`). UCF §7.6.5 already carries `:yin.k/primitives {name <expected profile>}` in the outcome.\\n- The lift's `discharge!` answers a qualified free name by registry presence (`rows.cljc:1611-1616`) and nothing of the entry travels. The task row's `requires` slot is a plain map (`rows.cljc:1687-1689`), so two more keys cost no slot change.\\n\\n### B.1 Ruling\\n\\n1. **Host modules participate in this slice.** Not deferred. Reason: `stream` and `cell`, the most common modules in any pack, are host modules; deferring leaves R6 (silent skew) open for the common case while closing it only for DHT-linked modules. The data is already pure, the comparison already exists in the linker, and the lift already resolves the entry. The risk of implementing is one more `requires` key and a fixture re-mint, both owed anyway for `:yin.k/modules`. The risk of deferring is a second re-mint later and a documented hole in the fetch-loop contract.\\n\\n2. **What the lift records.** Only what the live code uses: for every live free name `ns/f` that `discharge!` answered through the registry (`rows.cljc:1614-1616`, after `E`, store, primitives and installing names, which stay as they are):\\n   - `:yin.k/modules` gets `{ns <manifest address>}` when the entry is linked (`(:address entry)` non-nil), `{ns nil}` when it is host-registered;\\n   - `:yin.k/host-exports` gets `{ns/f <profile address>}` when the entry is host-registered, the value being `(module/host-export-profile (:modules m) 'ns/f)`.\\n   Not all exports. Recording all exports would refuse a receiver whose host module gained or changed an export the code never touches, and it would persist what the free-name scan already derives. A lift where `host-export-profile` answers nil for a name the registry claims to hold (an entry with a malformed `:yin.module/primitives`) is `:yin.k/non-portable :host-export-profile {:yin.k/name ns/f}`.\\n\\n3. **Canonical encoding.** Two maps in the task row's `requires` beside `:yin.k/segments`, `:yin.k/trees` and `:yin.k/cursor-profiles`: `:yin.k/modules {symbol -> string-or-nil}` and `:yin.k/host-exports {qualified-symbol -> keyword}`. Keys sorted by the carrier's existing rules for symbol keys; the `keyed`/`built` host-collapse discipline applies (module names contain dots, no slash; a qualified export has one slash, so the known P3 `keyed` gap does not reach these maps, but add the count guard anyway as the `built` precedent). Absent maps are not emitted when empty (same as `:yin.k/trees` with no segments is still emitted; follow whatever the existing `requires` does for empties, byte-stable). No richer value in `:yin.k/modules`: a tagged vector `[:host profiles]` beside address strings mixes value kinds in one slot and duplicates the primitives precedent for no gain.\\n\\n4. **How the lower compares** (new `check-modules!`, one pass over the whole tree, after `check-custody!`, before `attach-streams!`, absorbing today's `check-install-admission!`):\\n   - `:yin.k/modules {ns address}`: receiver's `module/resolve-module` entry exists with `(= address (:address entry))` → satisfied. Entry exists with another address (including a host entry, nil, where a linked one was pinned, or vice versa) → **terminal** `{:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied :yin.k/kind :module-pin-mismatch :yin.k/name ns :yin.k/pinned address :yin.k/linked (:address entry)}`, the `:dependency-pin-mismatch` words (`engine.cljc:1388-1393`). Entry absent → collected into `:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {ns address}}`.\\n   - `:yin.k/host-exports {ns/f profile}`: `(= profile (module/host-export-profile (:modules recv) 'ns/f))` → satisfied. Receiver answers another profile → **terminal** `{:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied :yin.k/kind :host-export-mismatch :yin.k/name ns/f :yin.k/pinned profile :yin.k/held <receiver's>}`. Receiver answers nil (no such export, or the module is absent, or it is linked rather than host) → collected into `:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/host-exports {ns/f profile}}` (the `:yin.k/modules {ns nil}` entry will be in the same map when the module is absent).\\n   - Receiver's host module exporting **more** than the pin names: satisfied (subset by construction, since only used exports are pinned). Equality is of profile addresses, never of normalised profile maps: the address already covers name, class, arities, effects and host-state.\\n   - Carried install children: `:yin.k/admitted-modules {ns address}` equality as today; unlisted → collected into `:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {ns carried-address}}`.\\n   - Order: terminal mismatches are thrown first (nothing the composition can fetch repairs them), then one collected refusal `{:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied :yin.k/discovery :complete :yin.k/missing {…}}` with keys present only where something is missing. Zero attaches in every case.\\n   - The fetch loop (composition, not this slice) requires only keys of `:yin.k/missing :yin.k/modules` whose pin is non-nil; a nil pin and every `:yin.k/host-exports` entry are composition prerequisites and are not fetched.\\n\\n5. **Determinism across hosts.** Profile addresses are BLAKE3 content hashes over plain data computed identically on all three hosts (the same mechanism Stage E already pins for primitives); manifest addresses are segment keys. The refusal maps are plain data. Pin T8 in `stage_e_rows_test.cljc`: a `requires` with both maps re-encodes byte-identically and the two terminal refusals and the collected refusal are `=` across JVM, Node and Dart.\\n\\n6. **Threat-model text amended by this ruling.** §4.2's shape gains `:yin.k/host-exports`; \\\"whose export profiles equal those the lift recorded\\\" becomes \\\"whose profile address for each used export equals the pinned one\\\"; §4.4's option is renamed `:yin.k/admitted-modules` and its refusal is folded into the collected shape with `:yin.k/discovery :complete`. T4 reads: a nil pin plus `:yin.k/host-exports` is satisfied by a host module answering equal profile addresses for the pinned exports; another profile for a pinned export refuses `:host-export-mismatch`; a missing export is collected as missing; extra exports are ignored.\\n\\n### B.2 Alternative considered and rejected\\n\\n\\\"Refuse nothing for nil pins, document, defer\\\": `:yin.k/modules {ns nil}` would then only assert \\\"a host module of this name must exist\\\", which `resolve-var` already enforces at run time, and skew in `stream`/`cell` profiles between two compositions would still run under R's authority (R6, R8 for the common case). The saving is one map and one lift line; not worth a second re-mint. Rejected.\\n\\n## Part C: ordered steps for codex round 2\\n\\nPreconditions: worktree `datomworld-srvm-pins`, the current 13 files uncommitted. `npm ci` and `mise trust` are done there. Per-iteration verification is `bb test:clj`; full three-host `bb test` once at the end, one lane set at a time, foreground only. Read `docs/agents/build-n-test.md` first. No `collab/` path is ever staged.\\n\\n**Commit 1 (R4, lands alone): fix P1-1, rename P2-2, ledger P2-1.**\\n1. `rows.cljc` `install-node`: `response` → `(dissoc response :yin.admit/id :yin.admit/decision :yin.admit/asserters :yin.admit/address)` before the `cbor/encode` check and the row. Delete the restore-side `dissoc` (`rows.cljc:2233-2237` and its comment).\\n2. `rows.cljc` `check-install!`: add to the existing `and` of the `:install-response` clause `(not-any? #(= \\\"yin.admit\\\" (namespace %)) (filter keyword? (keys response)))`.\\n3. Rename `:yin.k/admitted` → `:yin.k/admitted-modules` in `rows.cljc`, `export.cljc`, `rows_support.cljc`, `rows_test.cljc`, `rows_custody_test.cljc`, `export_test.cljc`, `safepoint_harness_test.cljc`.\\n4. Tests in `rows_test.cljc` `carried-install-requires-receiver-admission`: keep every assertion; add (a) the decoded wire's root `:install` row slot 3 has none of the four keys, (b) the harness-style relift of the lowered machine is `=` by root to the wire (reuse `canonical-under` or compare the install row), (c) a pack with the four keys spliced into the install row refuses `:yin.k/undecodable :install-response` with zero attaches. In `export_test.cljc`: a frozen parked-installer whose source response carried the sender record rehydrates `:ok` and reproduces the pack byte for byte (this is the P1-1 regression pin).\\n5. Mutants (run, record counts, restore): (m1) lift keeps the sender keys → 4(a), 4(b)/export pin fail; (m2) `check-install!` accepts `:yin.admit/*` keys → 4(c) fails; (m3) gate bypass → as before.\\n6. Docs (P3-3 list): reword \\\"dropped on restore\\\" to \\\"never carried by the lift; a carried one is refused\\\", rename the option, add the known-gaps row for P2-1 (holder driver seam, P2) and the P3-2 docstring note. Revisions I-8 wording likewise.\\n7. `bb test:clj`, kondo on changed files, `git diff --check`. Report; Architect sign-off; commit `fix(yin.vm.ucf): carried install children need receiver admission; lift never carries sender admission` (format.md convention, no Co-Authored-By).\\n\\n**Commit 2 (pins carrier + lift + lower + driver seam): the ruling.**\\n8. `rows.cljc` lift: in `discharge!` (or a sibling collector over the same `answered?` walk), record for every live registry-answered name the entry: linked → `:yin.k/modules {ns address}`; host → `:yin.k/modules {ns nil}` and `:yin.k/host-exports {ns/f profile}`; nil profile → `:yin.k/non-portable :host-export-profile`. Put both maps into `requires` (`rows.cljc:1687-1689`), sorted, empty maps handled as the existing `requires` keys handle empties.\\n9. Encoder/decoder/validator: `requires` is a plain map today, so confirm `check-dependencies!` (`rows.cljc:1918`) still accepts the two extra keys and add the key-count guard for symbol keys as in `built`. Malformed-slot collection: non-map `:yin.k/modules`, non-symbol key, non-string-non-nil value, non-keyword `:yin.k/host-exports` value, unqualified `:yin.k/host-exports` key → `:yin.k/undecodable :requires` (extend the existing kind, no new kind).\\n10. `rows.cljc` lower: replace `check-install-admission!` by `check-modules!` per B.1 item 4 (terminal mismatches first, then one collected refusal with `:yin.k/discovery :complete`, zero attaches), same position (after custody, before attach). Delete `check-install-admission!`.\\n11. Driver seam (P2-1): `driver/lowered` and the fenced recovery call forward `(:yin.k/admitted-modules (:config state))`; `rehydrate-fenced` already forwards. One driver test with and without the config over a parked-installer checkpoint.\\n12. Tests (threat model §7.1, amended): T1 (lift of harness row 17 emits `{:yin.k/modules {host.mod nil} :yin.k/host-exports {host.mod/f <profile>}}`; a DHT-linked fixture emits `{pym.k <address>}`; names answered by `E`, store, prims or module stores emit nothing), T2 (receiver lacking the module: collected refusal, `:discovery :complete`, zero attaches), T3 (linked module at another address: `:module-pin-mismatch` naming both; equal address lowers), T4 (B.1 item 6), T5 (already in commit 1, re-point to the collected shape), T8 (Stage E cross-host row), T9 (layering: `rows.cljc` requires neither `linker.interpreter`, `linker.dht` nor `dao.lease`), T10 (`resolve-var` unchanged). T6/T7 (fetch loop, lease) are composition work, out of this slice; leave their known-gaps rows.\\n13. Mutants (run, record, restore): lift records all exports instead of used; lower compares by name presence instead of address; lower accepts a different profile address; lower reports `:incomplete`; attach before `check-modules!`. Each must be killed by a named test.\\n14. Fixture re-mint: `rows-checkpoint-v3.txt` and any ledger/Stage E fixture whose `requires` now carries the two maps; record old → new addresses in the report and in `yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md` (I-8 completes, dated). C4 scanner pins are untouched (AST-level; see the standing note).\\n15. Docs: continuation §2.5 (binding fact travels: the two maps), §7.1 step 6 (records address or host profile), §7.2 dependencies row (module check, three refusal kinds, delete \\\"the lower does not re-discharge\\\"), §11 Q5 closed as C with the host-export ruling, Q3 (admitted set is `:yin.k/admitted-modules`); UCF §7.6.4 (add the host-export sentence), §7.6.5 (add `:yin.k/host-exports` to the outcome), §7.11 row updated; transport grammar (`requires` slot: the two maps); `yin.vm.linker.dht.md` 7.5.11 amendment reworded; threat-model report is a collab artifact, not edited; known-gaps: Q5 row → landed, R4 row → landed, P2-1 row → closed by step 11.\\n16. `bb test:clj` per iteration; at the end `bb test` all three hosts (foreground, one lane set at a time; \\\"Testing <ns>\\\" must appear in Node output); kondo; `git diff --check`. Report with counts, mutant kills, old → new addresses. Architect sign-off, then commit `feat(yin.vm.ucf): module pins and host-export pins in requires; lower re-discharges by equal address and profile` and, if the driver seam is separable, a third commit `feat(yin.vm.ucf.holder): admitted-modules config forwarded to the lower`.\\n\\nCommit split summary: (1) R4 alone, after the P1-1 fix and the rename; (2) carrier + lift + lower + tests + re-mint + docs; (3) optional driver seam if it would otherwise delay (2).\\n\\nCHANGES-REQUIRED (Part A)\\nRULING-READY\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/1793600000000-engineer-module-pins-r2c.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:16:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_6\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1793520000000-architect-fetch-threat-model.report.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"Created-GMT: 2026-10-17 03:00:00 GMT\\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-17 10:00:00 +07\\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-10-16 05:10:00 GMT\\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-16 12:10:00 +07\\nCoding-Agent: claude (claude-fable-5-1)\\nSession-ID: pending\\nRole: Architect (read-only; worktree datomworld-threat at 6df441d0 = origin/master)\\nBrief: collab/1793520000000-architect-fetch-threat-model.prompt.md\\n\\n# Threat model: policy-gated receiver-side fetch of modules a lowered continuation names (continuation §11 Q5)\\n\\n## 0. One-paragraph answer\\n\\nUsing the linker from the lower *can* enable injection, but not through the\\nlinker's own pipeline: the pipeline verifies address, identity, derivation,\\nmanifest name, declared obligations and (on the DHT path) asks the holder's\\nadmission policy before any load. The injection routes are around it:\\n(i) **name-only satisfaction** (today's `discharge!` and `resolve-var` match a\\nmodule by *name*, so a same-named module of other content at R silently\\nanswers; a fetch loop that requires by name inherits this), (ii) **carried\\ninstall children** (a pack's `:install` rows are verified self-consistent and\\nthen installed into R's registry family by `link-install` with S's admission\\nrecord copied, never R's policy asked), and (iii) **a composition that seeds\\nits name environment or `:trusted` derivation policy from carrier data**.\\nOption D (fetch inside symbol resolution) is correctly rejected. The verdict is\\n**C in UCF §7.6.4's existing form** (`:yin.k/modules {name manifest-address}`\\nin `requires`), with B's mechanism (re-discharge on lower, refuse before\\nattach, composition drives an explicit `require`, re-lower from the same\\npack) and the install-child admission gap closed in the same slice.\\n\\n## 1. Assets and trust boundaries\\n\\n### 1.1 What R protects\\n\\n| Asset | Where it lives | Why it matters for a fetch loop |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Module registry | `(:modules state)`, a value (`module.cljc:27`, linker I7 `yin.vm.linker.md:201`) | Exposure domain is the **installation family for its life**; a linked name answers later `require`s with no link request and no admission question (`yin.vm.linker.dht.md:2317-2333`); untrust is not retroactive (`:2335-2338`). Poisoning is sticky. |\\n| Program store | isolated per task; the pack's slice replaces it (UCF §7.6.2 `:1623-1640`); pinned by `rows_test.cljc:1170-1179` | Not reachable from a pack: receiver-only store/module-store state is discarded, the carried slice never merges. |\\n| Module stores | `:module-stores`, instantiated per task from the pack (`rows.cljc:2210-2213`) | Sender-chosen content; a closure with `store-of m` resolves names there **before** the registry (`engine.cljc:127-139`). Not a linker question: the pack carries code by design. |\\n| Streams | attached only by the composition's `attach!`; declined = `:yin.k/unsatisfied {:dao.stream/identity}` (`rows.cljc:2052-2061`) | A pack names identities, it cannot mint handles. |\\n| Authority and custody | grant, epoch, occurrence (UCF §7.7; `check-custody!` `rows.cljc:2008`) | A fetch that runs **after** the grant holds custody while it waits. |\\n| Linker budgets | `default-bounds` `{:max-parts 65536 :max-depth 256 :max-bytes 16MB}` (`linker.cljc:1321`); `fetch` has no deadline (`:1958-1960`) | Amplification and starvation surface. |\\n| Admission media | capacity 1024, evict-oldest (`yin.vm.linker.dht.md:2158-2163`) | Unanswered questions park links forever (`:2076-2086`). |\\n| Privacy | DHT `get`s for manifests and closures | The names a pack makes R fetch are visible to DHT peers. |\\n\\n### 1.2 Who is trusted, and for what\\n\\n| Party | Trusted for | Not trusted for |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| S (sender) | Nothing by default. Under exclusive custody, the grantor's record binds `:checkpoint` to the pack address (UCF §7.7, `rows.cljc:1928-1959`). A fork pack is unbound data. | Which code R should install; which names exist; which addresses they resolve to. |\\n| The carrier stream | Delivery and, when attached with an identity, attribution. Row ids and the pack address are BLAKE3 and re-verified at decode (continuation §7.2 `:1744`). | Authorship: the pack is not signed by S; integrity binds only to an address R must learn out of band (the grant) or not at all (fork). |\\n| The DHT | Integrity of content-addressed bytes: `:address-mismatch`/`:hash-mismatch` (`linker.cljc:1392-1394`, ingress `:1202-1221`). | Availability, naming, authority. A tuple in an index \\\"never establishes its own authority\\\" (`yin.vm.linker.dht.md:1748-1750`). |\\n| A module publisher | Only if **declared** (`--dht-principal`) does its assertion enter the fold; only if **trusted** does admission allow it (`:2292-2300`). Safety checks (L-e: profiles, pins, export origin) hold regardless (`:2342-2349`). | Anything when undeclared; code semantics even when trusted. |\\n| R's composition | Root of trust: `:authority`, `:admission` policy, `attach!`, the drive, the lease judge. | It must not import trust from the pack (names, addresses, derivation policy). |\\n\\n## 2. Attacker models\\n\\n| Id | Attacker | Capabilities | Cannot |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| M1 | Malicious sender | Chooses every row: code vectors, free names, module stores, install children with manifests/derivations/images, pins (option C), custody slots. | Forge a pack address a grant names; forge sealed resource refs (`:forged-resource-reference`, continuation §7.1 step 4); write R's ambient store. |\\n| M2 | Honest sender, hostile network | Replace or mutate a pack in flight; replay an old pack; delay. | Pass decode with a mutated row (digest refusal); pass custody for an exclusive root without the grant evidence. |\\n| M3 | Hostile DHT peer | Serve wrong or oversized content; withhold; serve slowly; serve a malformed closure. | Pass step 2/3 (address, identity); exceed `default-bounds`. |\\n| M4 | Hostile module publisher (declared principal) | Assert any name it likes under its key, including names another publisher uses; republish; equivocate. | Enter the fold undeclared; win an ambiguous name (`:ambiguous-name`, `yin.vm.linker.dht.md:1789-1791`); survive equivocation (`yin.vm.linker.md:2010-2018`); be admitted when untrusted. |\\n| M5 | Local malicious task | `require` any name; `try-require`; loop. | Write the registry except through install; reach `:resources` or the admission response medium; issue references without the task secret (`engine.cljc:1296-1301`). |\\n\\n## 3. Attack routes against options A-D\\n\\nOptions: **A** accept (composition prerequisite, today). **B** re-discharge on lower, refuse before attach with `:yin.k/unsatisfied {:yin.k/missing {:obligations …}}`, composition drives `require`, retries. **C** B plus the carrier pins the manifest address each registry-answered name resolved to at S; R satisfies only by equal address. **D** implicit fetch inside `resolve-var`.\\n\\nCode facts the table relies on (all read):\\n- Lift `discharge!` answers a namespaced name by **presence** in S's registry, `(some? (module/resolve-module …))` (`rows.cljc:1615-1617`); nothing of the entry travels (continuation §2.5 `:360-366`).\\n- Lower `check-dependencies!` checks segments, trees, store census, `attaches?`, closure origin/binders, `:prim` presence (`rows.cljc:1898-1925`); **no registry check** (continuation §7.2 `:1827-1830`). `restore-task` keeps `recv`'s `:modules` (`rows.cljc:2095-2099`; pinned at `rows_test.cljc:1168-1169`).\\n- Runtime `resolve-var` resolves by name through the registry (`engine.cljc:133-139`), else `Unable to resolve symbol` (`:140`); called from the semantic evaluator with `(:modules machine)` (`semantic.cljc:152`).\\n- The link-pair interpreter serves **by-name requests only** (`interpreter.cljc:483-486`), resolves through R's fold, asks admission after resolve and before load (`:437-462`), loads the **retained** address of the allow (`:412-413`), and `settle` re-checks the manifest's name (`engine.cljc:1540-1548`) and runs 5b against live state (`:1214-1237`).\\n\\n| # | Route | Precondition | Impact | Mitigated today? (cite) | Residual under A | under B | under C | under D |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| R1 | **Name squatting / dependency confusion at R** (M4, M1): R holds or resolves `pym.k` to content other than S's. | A same-named module in R's registry, or a declared+trusted principal asserting the name. | Continuation runs against other code; silent semantic substitution, with the pack's effects authorised under R's streams. | Partly: the fold refuses ambiguity and unauthenticated envelopes (`yin.vm.linker.md:2065-2078`); admission refuses untrusted asserters. **Not** mitigated for a name R already holds: `resolve-var` has no address check; the pin invariant covers only manifest-declared `:yin.module/requires` (`module.cljc:113-142`), never a continuation's free name. | **High**: skew undetected. | **High**: name-present passes the re-discharge. | **Closed**: equal-address check (as `declared-discharge` `:module`, `linker.cljc:1021-1027`; UCF §7.6.4 `:1699-1702`). | High, plus implicit. |\\n| R2 | **Carrier-driven fetch** (M1): pack names free symbols chosen to make R fetch. | A composition fetch loop. | R issues DHT loads and admission questions for attacker-chosen names; cost, leak, parked links. | No loop exists today. The linker side bounds one fetch (`default-bounds`) and asks admission per name (`:2037-2049`). `:composition` provenance is **not asked** (`interpreter.cljc:447`). | None (no fetch). | **Medium**: loop runs by name; bounded by distinct names in the pack (decode budget) and by R's policy. | **Medium→Low**: a pin lets the loop refuse before fetching when R's own resolution disagrees (one fold, no load). | **High**: every `:var` may fetch; no explicit effect. |\\n| R3 | **Identity substitution** (M3, M4): wrong bytes for an address, or a manifest whose derivation does not lead to its image. | Hostile content source. | Would install unverified code. | **Yes**: steps 2/3 (`linker.cljc:1392`), manifest name (`:2400-2404`), derivation `:verifying` (`:2164-2216`), `foreign-image` at install (`engine.cljc:1415-1422`), `check-install!` for carried children (`rows.cljc:1853-1858`). | Low | Low | Low | Low |\\n| R4 | **Carried install child bypasses R's admission** (M1). | Pack carries an `:install` row (semantic kernel accepts; backends refuse `:installs`, continuation §7.2 `:1760`). | After the child halts at R, `link-install` receives the module into R's registry **family** with **S's** `:admission` record copied (`engine.cljc:1436-1443`); later `require`s answer from the registry, never asked. **Registry poisoning via the carrier.** | **No.** `check-install!` verifies self-consistency only; the design says binding to composition-known addresses \\\"remains the linker's fetch/admission responsibility\\\" (continuation §11 Q3 `:2744-2745`) and no one performs it at lower. Only the sealed child secret (`:secret-source`) and L-e checks apply. | **High** (exists today, independent of Q5) | High unless fixed | **Closed if** carried installs pass the same equal-address + R-admission rule (§4.4). | n/a |\\n| R5 | **TOCTOU between check and fetch/install** (M5, race): registry changes between the refusal and the re-lower. | Another task links the same name meanwhile. | Re-lower sees name present (B) → skew; or install races a concurrent install (`:installs` join, `engine.cljc:1536`). | Lower is pure over a `recv` value and attaches nothing on refusal (attach-count law, continuation §7.2 `:1800-1803`). First link wins for module stores (`engine.cljc:1107-1108`). | n/a | **Medium**: name-present check is race-sensitive. | **Low**: equality against the pin is race-insensitive; the composition re-lowers from the same bytes. | High |\\n| R6 | **Version skew, same name different code at S and R** (honest both). | Different snapshot sets or principals at S and R. | Wrong behaviour, not detectable at run time. | No. | High | High | **Closed** (refuse `:yin.k/module-pin-mismatch` naming both addresses). | High |\\n| R7 | **Fetch amplification and cycles** (M1, M3). | Many names; deep closures; mutually requiring modules. | CPU, bytes, parked links. | Per-fetch `default-bounds`; `:parts-limit` (`linker.cljc:1349`); `:require-cycle` on install ancestry (`module.cljc:592-599`); transitive requires are the child's own requests. **No** bound on the number of requires a composition issues, **no** deadline (`fetch` `:1958`; link-policy `:lease` deferred, `yin.repl.link-policy.md:156-160`). | None | **Medium**: needs a per-run budget and lease (§4.3). | Medium, same | High |\\n| R8 | **Side effect before failure** (A's runtime symptom). | A missing name reached after an effect. | Partial execution under R's authority; under exclusive custody the occurrence is consumed and a terminal/successor edge is owed (`yin.vm.linker.dht.md:4137-4157`). | No: A fails at `engine.cljc:140` at run time. | **High** | **Closed** (refuse before attach). | Closed | Closed only if the fetch succeeds; otherwise a mid-run park with network. |\\n| R9 | **Information leak through fetch requests** (M3 observers). | Fetch loop over the DHT. | Peers learn which modules R resumes; admission medium learns names too (by design). | DHT `get` is inherent; `:manual` link policy lets the holder decline. | None | **Low-Medium**: composition policy decides; pins allow a local-only check first. | Low-Medium | High (unconsented) |\\n| R10 | **Registry poisoning** (M1 via R4; M4 via trust). | See R4; or a trusted malicious principal. | Family-wide, lifetime. | For M4: admission is the designed control; L-e safety floor. For M1: **not mitigated** (R4). | High | High | Closed with R4 fix | n/a |\\n| R11 | **Policy bypass of `:admit`/ShiBi** (composition error, M1-induced). | Loop satisfies a missing name through `:name-env` (provenance `:composition`, never asked, `yin.vm.linker.dht.md:2008`) or a non-DHT source. | Admission skipped for carrier-chosen names. | The seam is sound; the bypass is a composition choice. Nothing today forbids seeding `:name-env` from a pack. | n/a | **Medium**: must be forbidden in the loop contract (§4.2). | Medium, same rule; the pin never substitutes for admission. | High |\\n| R12 | **Downgrade** (composition error). | Loop links under `:derivation :trusted` (`linker.cljc:2504-2519`) or against a `:fallback` format. | Derivation unverified for carrier-named modules. | `:trusted` is meant for a composition that is its own publisher (`yin.vm.linker.md:1096-1102`). | n/a | Medium | Medium | High |\\n| R13 | **Replay / substitution of the pack itself** (M2). | Fork packs, or a receiver that does not check the grant's `:checkpoint`. | An old or attacker-built pack lowers. | Exclusive: grant names the pack address (`rows.cljc:1928-1959`). Fork: out of scope of this question; a fork is data the composition chose to run. | Same in all options; a fetch loop must bind its retry to **one** pack address (§4.3). |\\n\\n## 4. Required mechanisms for a safe policy-gated fetch loop\\n\\n### 4.1 Who decides\\n\\n- **The lower decides nothing and fetches nothing.** It reports, before any\\n  attach, the complete set of unsatisfied module bindings. Pure, no stream, no\\n  clock (as today for segments, trees, stores, prims).\\n- **The receiving composition decides**, as holder context of R's registry and\\n  owner of the link pair, the authority, the admission policy and the drive.\\n  It may answer \\\"no\\\" (manual policy) and the pack stays refused.\\n- **The carrier narrows, never widens.** A pin (C) can only make R refuse\\n  what R would otherwise have accepted by name. It grants nothing: the fetch\\n  still goes by **name** through R's fold and R's admission, and the installed\\n  entry's address must then equal the pin.\\n- **The VM never learns any of this** (I6 `yin.vm.linker.md:196-199`).\\n\\n### 4.2 The refusal outcome the lower must carry (exact shape)\\n\\n```clojure\\n{:yin.k/status    :yin.k/unsatisfied\\n :yin.k/discovery :complete                     ; the set below is exhaustive (one pass over all contexts)\\n :yin.k/missing   {:yin.k/modules {pym.k :segment/blake3-…    ; C: the address S's registry held\\n                                   host.mod nil}              ; a name S answered from a host module (no address)\\n                   :obligations  #{pym.k/body host.mod/f}}}   ; the free names, as today\\n```\\n\\n- Keys are plain data, sorted by the carrier's rules; no symbol-to-string\\n  host collapse (one entry per module name).\\n- `:yin.k/modules` values: the manifest address (`:address` of the registry\\n  entry, `module.cljc:92`) for a linked module; `nil` for a host-registered\\n  module (`register-host-module` entries carry no address). A `nil` pin is\\n  satisfied by a host module of that name whose export profiles equal those\\n  the lift recorded (reuse `module/host-export-profile`, `module.cljc:266`),\\n  else refused. A composition that cannot supply the host module cannot\\n  fetch it: host modules are composition prerequisites and stay so.\\n- The composition drives the loop **without trusting names**: it requires\\n  the key (a name) through its own link pair, the admission question carries\\n  R's fold's address and asserters, and after `linked` it compares\\n  `(:address entry)` with the pin. Mismatch is terminal:\\n  `{:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied :yin.k/kind :module-pin-mismatch\\n  :yin.k/name pym.k :yin.k/pinned … :yin.k/linked …}` (same words as\\n  `:dependency-pin-mismatch`, `engine.cljc:1388-1393`).\\n- Forbidden in the loop: adding `:name-env` entries from the pack; switching\\n  `:derivation` to `:trusted`; passing `:fallback` formats the pack named;\\n  requiring anything not in `:yin.k/modules`.\\n\\n### 4.3 Budgets, deadlines, atomicity\\n\\n- **Budget**: at most one `require` per key of `:yin.k/modules`, at most two\\n  `lower-task` calls per pack address per attempt (refuse, then re-lower).\\n  Transitive requirements are the install child's own (`yin.vm.linker.md:1788-1797`)\\n  and stay inside the linker's existing bounds and cycle refusal.\\n- **Deadline**: a `dao.lease` over the whole fetch run, subject\\n  `[:yin.k/lower pack-address]` (per-run, link-policy.md §7 Q2), holder the\\n  composition's drive, renewal on every round that made progress\\n  (`round`'s `:progress?`, `interpreter.cljc:521-523`), judge composed in the\\n  process that owns the link pair, reclaim = `abandon`/`retire` of every\\n  link the run owns (`interpreter/retire` by run descriptor,\\n  `yin.vm.linker.dht.md:2088-2129`) plus dropping the pack. `:cap` gives the\\n  hard ceiling. No host clock in the loop; ticks are data (`dao.lease.md:104-112`).\\n- **Order relative to custody**: fetch **before** proposing for the grant.\\n  UCF 14.2.3 step 2 already puts \\\"requirements\\\" before the proposal\\n  (`yin.vm.linker.dht.md:4115-4119`). A stuck fetch therefore holds no\\n  tenure, mints no occurrence and owes no successor. Only the final\\n  re-lower runs under the grant, and it is pure and fast.\\n- **Atomicity**: the lower is a pure function of `(recv, wire)`; the\\n  composition passes the **same wire bytes** and a `recv` whose registry is\\n  the value it observed after the installs. Because satisfaction is by equal\\n  address, a concurrent change to the registry cannot turn a refusal into a\\n  wrong acceptance; at worst it turns it into another refusal.\\n- **Idempotence**: a repeated loop over one pack address is a no-op once the\\n  entries are present (registry answers without a link request).\\n\\n### 4.4 Carried install children (closes R4)\\n\\nA pack's `:install` row names a manifest address. The lower must refuse the\\nchild unless the receiving composition **admits that address for that name**,\\nby the same equal-address rule: the composition resolves the name in its own\\nfold, asks its admission policy (question = name, address, asserters, as\\ntoday), and passes the admitted set to the lower as data\\n(`opts {:yin.k/admitted {pym.k :segment/…}}`); an unlisted child is\\n`:yin.k/unsatisfied {:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {pym.k <carried address>}}}`\\nbefore any attach. Default empty set = fail closed. The copied `:admission`\\nrecord from S (`engine.cljc:1436-1443`) is then evidence of S's decision only\\nand must be replaced by R's at `link-install` (or dropped).\\n\\n### 4.5 What the composition must verify, as a checklist\\n\\n1. Pack address equals the grant's `:checkpoint` (exclusive) or a value it\\n   chose itself (fork).\\n2. Every key of `:yin.k/modules` was required through its **own** link pair\\n   under a DHT or content source it configured; none through `:name-env`\\n   seeded from the pack.\\n3. Every resulting entry carries `:admission` from **R's** policy or\\n   provenance `:composition` chosen by R, and `(:address entry)` equals the pin.\\n4. The re-lower is called with the same wire and a `recv` built from the\\n   registry value observed in step 3.\\n5. The lease was live throughout; a lapse retires the run and the pack is\\n   not re-lowered until a fresh attempt.\\n\\n## 5. What must NOT live in the VM or the lower (D confirmed rejected)\\n\\n- **No fetch in `resolve-var`.** It would make every `:var` instruction an\\n  implicit network operation (invariants: no implicit control flow, callbacks\\n  are stream events; I4 no operation waits, `yin.vm.linker.md:179-182`; I6 the\\n  VM never invokes a loader, `:196-199`). The custody gate stops link\\n  requests under `:exporting` (`module.cljc:541-543`); a resolve-time fetch\\n  would have to re-invent that discipline inside the evaluator.\\n- **No admission context in the VM.** \\\"Who is asking\\\" is composition-owned\\n  holder context, never a datum (`yin.vm.linker.dht.md:2248-2255`); the VM\\n  has none to give.\\n- **No clock, no lease, no budget in the lower.** The lower is pure and\\n  portable; liveness is `dao.lease`'s and the drive's (`linker.cljc:1958-1960`).\\n- **No name environment or trust in the carrier.** A pack may pin an address\\n  (a fact of S's state); it may not assert who may bind a name (a pinned\\n  address \\\"is never a name claim\\\", `yin.vm.linker.dht.md:1835-1837`).\\n- **No registry entries in the row table.** Code travels as segments; a\\n  module's installed slice does not travel (continuation §2.5 `:360-366`\\n  stands); only the binding fact `name → address` travels.\\n- **No language, frontend or session key** anywhere in the new shape\\n  (`yin.vm.linker.dht.md:2302-2316`).\\n\\n## 6. Verdict on Q5\\n\\n**C**, implemented as B plus one map, in UCF's already-specified shape.\\n\\n- **A is unacceptable.** It has the only runtime symptom in the gap list\\n  (`collab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md:125`), it fails\\n  **after** effects under R's authority (R8), and it hides version skew (R1,\\n  R6) completely.\\n- **B alone is insufficient.** Refusing before attach fixes R8 but keeps\\n  name-only satisfaction, so dependency confusion (R1), skew (R6) and the\\n  TOCTOU on name presence (R5) remain, and a fetch loop driven by names\\n  gives M1 a free hand to choose what R loads (R2) subject only to R's trust\\n  set.\\n- **C's format change is justified.** UCF §7.6.4 already requires\\n  `:yin.k/modules` keyed by manifest address with equal-address\\n  satisfaction (`:1697-1702`) and §7.6.5 already lists it in the outcome\\n  (`:1716-1718`); the row carrier dropped it (continuation §2.5). \\\"Derive,\\n  don't persist\\\" does not apply: the binding S's registry held is a fact of\\n  S's state that no query over R's rows can recover. Cost: one map entry per\\n  registry-answered name in the task row's `requires` slot; the lift already\\n  resolves the entry (`rows.cljc:1616`) and only has to keep its `:address`.\\n  Packs re-mint (recorded in `yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md`); no backward\\n  compatibility is owed.\\n- **Pin, do not fetch by identity.** By-address link requests are refused by\\n  the interpreter (`interpreter.cljc:483-486`) and admission has no asserter\\n  for a bare address. Keep the fetch by name through R's fold and admission;\\n  use the pin only as the equality the lower and the loop check. This keeps\\n  \\\"A is the only code identity\\\" intact: the pin is a manifest content address,\\n  a claim about S's binding, not a new code identity.\\n- **R4 lands in the same slice.** It is the actual injection route in today's\\n  code and it is the same check (equal address, R-admitted) applied to\\n  carried install children.\\n\\n## 7. Tests and pins (portable, cljc) and documentation\\n\\n### 7.1 Tests\\n\\n| # | Pin | Where |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| T1 | Lift of harness row 17 (`safepoint_harness_test.cljc:397-409`, `host.mod/f` through the registry) emits `requires {:yin.k/modules {host.mod <address>}}`; a name answered by `E`, the store or a module store emits no entry. | `rows_test.cljc` |\\n| T2 | Lower into a receiver lacking `host.mod` throws `:yin.k/unsatisfied :yin.k/discovery :complete :yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {host.mod <address>} :obligations #{host.mod/f}}` with **zero** `attach!` calls (attach-count law). | `rows_test.cljc` |\\n| T3 | Lower into a receiver holding `host.mod` at another `:address` throws `:module-pin-mismatch` naming both addresses, zero attaches. Receiver at the equal address lowers. | `rows_test.cljc` |\\n| T4 | A `nil` pin (host module) is satisfied only by equal export profiles; a same-named host module with another profile refuses. | `rows_test.cljc` |\\n| T5 | A carried `:install` child whose manifest address is not in `opts :yin.k/admitted` refuses before attach; listed, it lowers; after `link-install` at R the entry's `:admission` is R's, not the carried one. | `rows_test.cljc` + `linker_require_test.cljc` |\\n| T6 | Loop test with a scripted composition: refusal → one `require` per key → admission medium holds exactly one question per key with R's fold's address → re-lower succeeds from the same bytes. Mutants killed: loop that seeds `:name-env` from the pack (no question appended → test fails); loop that passes `:derivation :trusted` (response `:trust :composition` → test fails). | new `ucf/fetch_loop_test.cljc` |\\n| T7 | Scripted-tick lease: a loop whose link never answers lapses `:silence` and retires every run-owned request; no grant was proposed; a second attempt is a fresh run. | same, with `dao.lease` fixtures (`lease_test.cljc` style) |\\n| T8 | Cross-host: the refusal map is `=` and re-encodes byte-identically on JVM, Node, Dart (Stage E row). | `stage_e_rows_test.cljc` |\\n| T9 | Layering: `yin.vm.engine`, `yin.vm.semantic*`, `yin.vm.ucf.rows` require neither `yin.vm.linker.interpreter` nor `yin.vm.linker.dht` nor `dao.lease` (D stays rejected by construction). | `layering_test.clj` |\\n| T10 | `resolve-var` unchanged: a name absent from env/store/prims/registry still fails with `Unable to resolve symbol`; no fetch, no park. | `engine` tests |\\n\\n### 7.2 Documentation\\n\\n- **continuation §2.5**: replace \\\"Linked registry entries do not travel …\\n  composition prerequisite\\\" with: the entry does not travel; the **binding\\n  fact** does, as `:yin.k/modules {name manifest-address|nil}` in\\n  `requires`; the receiver's registry is kept as given and must satisfy each\\n  binding by equal address (host modules by export profile).\\n- **continuation §7.1 step 6**: the registry step records the entry's\\n  address. **§7.2 dependencies row**: add the module check and the two\\n  refusal kinds; delete \\\"The lower does not re-discharge free names\\\"\\n  (`:1827-1830`) and the §7.1 sentence at `:1700-1701`. **§11 Q5**: closed\\n  as C; **Q3**: amend \\\"remains the linker's responsibility\\\" to the admitted\\n  set passed to the lower.\\n- **UCF §7.6.4/7.6.5**: no change in substance; note the row carrier now\\n  implements it. **§7.11**: add a blocker row \\\"Receiver-side module\\n  satisfaction and carried-install admission: lower refuses before attach;\\n  the fetch loop is the composition's, leased, before the grant proposal;\\n  tests T1-T10\\\". Cross-reference 14.2.3 step 2 for ordering.\\n- **yin.vm.linker.dht.md 7.5.11**: add that a lowered pack's install child\\n  enters the family only through R's admission.\\n- **known-gaps**: one row for R4 (P1 until the slice lands), one for the\\n  missing per-run lease (P2, reserved `:lease` policy).\\n\\nTHREAT-MODEL-READY\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/1793600000000-engineer-module-pins-r2c.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:17:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_7\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '140,240p' collab/1793550000000-architect-module-pins-review.report.md; rg -n 'requires|discharge\\\"'!|check-install-admission|check-dependencies|defn.*keyed|defn.*built'\\\"' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\ncollab/1793600000000-engineer-module-pins-r2c.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:18:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_7\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '140,240p' collab/1793550000000-architect-module-pins-review.report.md; rg -n 'requires|discharge\\\"'!|check-install-admission|check-dependencies|defn.*keyed|defn.*built'\\\"' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"1011:(defn- keyed-node\\n1063:(defn- decode-keyed\\n1595:(defn- discharge!\\n1685:        _ (discharge! ctx code)\\n1690:        requires {:yin.k/cursor-profiles (if (seq (:cells acc)) remote/cursor-profiles #{})\\n1694:                          (node :cursor-cells (mapcat identity (:cells acc))) requires code installs waits\\n1887:(defn- check-install-admission!\\n1914:(defn- check-dependencies!\\n1915:  \\\"Step 9, dependency closure: requires and code agree, every segment has\\n1921:  (let [[_ _ _ _ _ _ _ module-stores _ _ requires code] (:slots task)]\\n1922:    (when-not (and (map? requires) (= (set (:yin.k/segments requires)) (set (keys code))))\\n1923:      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :requires {}))\\n1924:    (let [trees (:yin.k/trees requires)\\n2301:     (doseq [step [check-stores! check-pendings! check-dependencies!]\\n2306:         (check-install-admission! t opts))\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/1793600000000-engineer-module-pins-r2c.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:20:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_8\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1,200p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; sed -n '1500,1730p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; sed -n '1780,1970p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"(ns yin.vm.ucf.rows\\n  \\\"Version-3 row codec. Pure row construction, graph decoding and\\n   discovery-order cursor-cell numbering (design note §1), then full task\\n   transport for the semantic kernel (continuation design §7):\\n   lift-task walks a quiescent machine into an abstract task and emits it;\\n   lower-task decodes, checks and restores one into a fresh receiver.\\n   An abstract row is {:kind keyword :slots vector}. Structural references\\n   contain abstract rows; values use [:lit d], [:row abstract-row], [:cursor-cell id].\\n   A task's :cursor-cells row holds alternating source identities and :cursor-cell-body\\n   rows. Install children are separate tasks with separate cursor-cell scopes.\\n\\n   The census is ordered numerically by n (draft §3, \\\\\\\"sorted by n\\\\\\\"), so\\n   :yin.k/cc-10 follows :yin.k/cc-9; its keys must spell cc-N with no leading\\n   zero, else :slot-kind.\\n\\n   Default value markers are plain maps {:yin.k/row abstract-row} and\\n   {:yin.k/cursor-cell keyword}. A guest map whose sole key is :yin.k/row or\\n   :yin.k/cursor-cell collides with them and is not portable: on encode and decode\\n   every literal of that shape is refused :yin.k/non-portable. Explicit\\n   markers use the caller value encoder.\\\"\\n  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\\n            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\\n            [yin.vm.semantic.analysis :as analysis]\\n            [yin.vm.semantic.code :as code]\\n            [yin.vm.semantic.frame :as frame]\\n            [yin.vm.semantic.scan :as scan]\\n            [yin.vm.ucf.custody :as custody]\\n            [yin.vm.ucf.remote :as remote]))\\n\\n\\n(def profile {:yin.code/contract \\\"v4\\\" :yin.k/version 1})\\n\\n\\n(def pending-table\\n  {:next [:C]\\n   :put [[:ref :stream] :V :D]\\n   :ffi [:C :D :D]\\n   :ffi-request [:D :V [:ref :stream] [:ref :stream] :C :D]\\n   :link-request [:D :S [:ref :stream] [:ref :stream] :C :D :D :D]\\n   :link-response [:D :S [:ref :stream] [:ref :stream] :C :D]\\n   :install [:S :D]})\\n\\n\\n(def row-table\\n  \\\"Slot descriptors, excluding id and kind. :repeat/:pairs are variadic;\\n   :refs is an ordered vector of structural references. :pending is\\n   discriminated by pending-table. Nothing in this table is executable.\\\"\\n  {:vec [:repeat :V] :list [:repeat :V] :set [:repeat :V]\\n   :map [:pairs :V :V] :bindings [:pairs :S :V] :store [:pairs :D :V]\\n   :env [[:ref :bindings] :optional-D]\\n   :closure [:A :N :syms [:ref :bindings] :optional-D]\\n   :prim [:S] :stream [:D :D] :reified [[:ref :act]] :parked-ref [:D]\\n   :act [:A :N [:ref :env] [:ref :window] [:ref :k] :N]\\n   :tail [:A :N [:ref :k]]\\n   :window [:pairs :N :V] :k [:repeat [:ref :kframe]]\\n   :kframe [:A :N [:ref :env] [:ref :window] :N]\\n   :wait [[:ref :act :tail] [:ref :pending]] :pending :pending\\n   :module-store [:D [:ref :store]]\\n   :parked-table [:pairs :D [:ref :act :tail]]\\n   :install [:S :D :D :D [:ref :task]]\\n   :cursor-cells [:pairs :C [:ref :cursor-cell-body]] :cursor-cell-body [[:ref :stream] :D]\\n   :task [:N :D :D :D :N [:ref :bindings] [:ref :store]\\n          [:refs :module-store] [:ref :parked-table] [:ref :cursor-cells]\\n          :D :D [:refs :install] [:refs :wait] :optional-D :optional-V :optional-D]})\\n\\n\\n(defn node\\n  [kind slots]\\n  {:kind kind :slots (if (= :window kind)\\n                       (vec (mapcat identity (sort-by first (partition 2 slots))))\\n                       (vec slots))})\\n\\n\\n(defn- refuse!\\n  [status kind path]\\n  (throw (ex-info \\\"Row codec refused data\\\"\\n                  {:yin.k/status status :yin.k/kind kind :yin.k/path path})))\\n\\n\\n(defn- bad!\\n  [kind path]\\n  (refuse! :yin.k/undecodable kind path))\\n\\n\\n(defn- marker-shaped?\\n  [x]\\n  (and (map? x) (= 1 (count x)) (or (contains? x :yin.k/row) (contains? x :yin.k/cursor-cell))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- check-literal-markers!\\n  [x]\\n  (when (marker-shaped? x) (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :marker []))\\n  (when (coll? x)\\n    (doseq [v (if (map? x) (mapcat identity x) x)] (check-literal-markers! v)))\\n  (when (meta x) (check-literal-markers! (meta x))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- bytes-key\\n  [bs]\\n  ;; Unsigned bytewise order, without a length-first comparison.\\n  (mapv #(bit-and (int %) 255) (seq bs)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- compare-bytes\\n  [a b]\\n  (loop [i 0]\\n    (cond\\n      (= i (count a)) (if (= i (count b)) 0 -1)\\n      (= i (count b)) 1\\n      (= (nth a i) (nth b i)) (recur (inc i))\\n      :else (compare (nth a i) (nth b i)))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- byte-compare\\n  [a b]\\n  (compare-bytes (bytes-key (cbor/encode a)) (bytes-key (cbor/encode b))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- sorted-bytes\\n  [xs]\\n  (vec (sort byte-compare xs)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- descriptors\\n  [kind slots]\\n  ;; :entry is the numbering's synthetic map entry [:entry k v], never a carrier row.\\n  (let [schema (if (= :entry kind) [:V :V] (get row-table kind))]\\n    (cond\\n      (= schema :pending) (into [:D] (get pending-table (first slots)))\\n      (= :repeat (first schema)) (vec (repeat (count slots) (second schema)))\\n      (= :pairs (first schema)) (vec (take (count slots) (cycle (rest schema))))\\n      :else schema)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- ref?\\n  [d]\\n  (and (vector? d) (= :ref (first d))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- refs?\\n  [d]\\n  (and (vector? d) (= :refs (first d))))\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private census-key #\\\"cc-([1-9][0-9]*)\\\")\\n\\n\\n(defn- census-order\\n  ;; Numeric order of cc-N without reading wire data: fewer digits first,\\n  ;; then the digits. Other keys (a partial emit-numbered) sort last.\\n  [k]\\n  (let [digits (when (keyword? k) (second (re-matches census-key (name k))))]\\n    (if digits [0 (count digits) digits] [1 0 (str k)])))\\n\\n\\n(defn- ordered-slots\\n  [kind slots]\\n  (cond\\n    (= kind :window) (vec (mapcat identity (sort-by first (partition 2 slots))))\\n    (= kind :cursor-cells) (vec (mapcat identity (sort-by #(census-order (first %)) (partition 2 slots))))\\n    (contains? #{:map :bindings :store :parked-table} kind)\\n    (vec (mapcat identity (sort #(byte-compare (first %1) (first %2)) (partition 2 slots))))\\n    (= kind :set) (sorted-bytes slots)\\n    :else slots))\\n\\n\\n(def default-budget\\n  \\\"Local resource bounds, independent of canonical bytes. :work counts the\\n   numbering's positions and the representation bound of every value it\\n   encodes for a comparison (design note §1.5).\\\"\\n  {:rows 10000 :cursor-cells 64 :depth 256 :work 4194304 :bytes 16777216})\\n\\n\\n(declare emit-node canonical-numbering child-numberer validate-frames)\\n\\n\\n(defn- emit-slot\\n  [d x numbering rows path number-child]\\n  (when-not (or (ref? d) (refs? d) (= :C d))\\n    (check-literal-markers! (if (contains? #{:V :optional-V} d)\\n                              (when (= :lit (first x)) (second x)) x)))\\n  (cond\\n    (ref? d) (emit-node x numbering rows path number-child)\\n    (refs? d) (reduce (fn [[out rs] [j n]]\\n                        (let [p (conj path (if (= :install (:kind n)) (first (:slots n)) j))\\n                              [id rs'] (emit-node n numbering rs p number-child)]\\n                          [(conj out id) rs']))\\n                      [[] rows] (map-indexed vector x))\\n    (= d :C) [(get numbering x x) rows]\\n    (contains? #{:V :optional-V} d)\\n    (case (first x)\\n      :row (let [[id rs] (emit-node (second x) numbering rows path number-child)] [[:row id] rs])\\n      :cursor-cell [[:cursor-cell (get numbering (second x) (second x))] rows]\\n      [x rows])\\n    :else [x rows]))\\n  (node :k (mapv (fn [f]\\n                   (let [a (address! ctx (:segment f))]\\n                     (context! ctx a (:pc f) (:env f))\\n                     (node :kframe [a (:pc f) (lift-env-node ctx (:env f))\\n                                    (window-node ctx (:window f)) (:rd f)])))\\n                 (or k []))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- state-node\\n  \\\"An evaluator payload (wait entry, parked record, reified payload) as\\n   its :act or :tail row; engine fields are the pending's.\\\"\\n  [ctx p]\\n  (if (contains? p :site)\\n    ;; a tail state resumes through its K: its own segment never runs again\\n    (node :tail [(address! ctx (:segment p)) (:site p) (k-node ctx (:k p))])\\n    (let [a (address! ctx (:segment p))]\\n      (context! ctx a (:pc p) (:env p))\\n      (node :act [a (:pc p) (lift-env-node ctx (:env p))\\n                  (window-node ctx (:window p)) (k-node ctx (:k p)) (get-in p [:deliver :rd])]))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- pending-node\\n  \\\"The observed wait's pending (draft §5.3): the reason is the entry's,\\n   never the site's static kind.\\\"\\n  [ctx e]\\n  (let [m (:m ctx)]\\n    (case (:reason e)\\n      :next (if (contains? e :call-id)\\n              (node :pending [:ffi (cell-for! ctx (get-in e [:cursor-ref :id])) (:call-id e) (:op e)])\\n              (node :pending [:next (cell-for! ctx (get-in e [:cursor-ref :id]))]))\\n      :put (if (:request-sent e)\\n             (let [carried? (and (:response-cursor e) (:response-stream e))\\n                   cursor (if carried? (:response-cursor e) vm/call-out-cursor-key)\\n                   response (if carried? (:response-stream e) vm/call-out-stream-key)]\\n               (when-not (get (:resources m) cursor) (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {}))\\n               (node :pending [:ffi-request (:call-id e) (lift-value ctx (:datom e)) (stream-row! ctx (:stream-id e))\\n                               (stream-row! ctx response) (cell-for! ctx cursor) (:op-id e)]))\\n             (do (when-not (contains? e :datom) (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :incomplete-write {}))\\n                 (node :pending [:put (stream-row! ctx (:stream-id e)) (lift-value ctx (:datom e)) (:op-id e)])))\\n      (:link-request :link-response)\\n      (let [c (cell! ctx [(:response e) (:cursor e)] (:response e) (:cursor e))\\n            base [(:reason e) (:link-id e) (:name e) (stream-row! ctx (:request e)) (stream-row! ctx (:response e)) c]]\\n        (node :pending (conj (if (= :link-request (:reason e)) (conj base (:envelope e) (:op-id e)) base)\\n                             (boolean (:try? e)))))\\n      :install (do (when-not (contains? (:installs m) (:name e))\\n                     (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :incomplete-install {:yin.k/name (:name e)}))\\n                   (node :pending [:install (:name e) (boolean (:try? e))]))\\n      (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :reason-mismatch {:yin.k/reason (:reason e)}))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- store-node\\n  [ctx s]\\n  (node :store (mapcat (fn [[k v]]\\n                         (when-not (= :lit (first (lift-value ctx k)))\\n                           (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :store-key {}))\\n                         [k (lift-value ctx v)])\\n                       s)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- module-store-nodes\\n  \\\"Every module store an environment or closure reaches, transitively.\\\"\\n  [ctx]\\n  (loop [done {}]\\n    (if-let [mid (first (sort-by str (remove #(contains? done %) (:stores @(:acc ctx)))))]\\n      (let [stores (:module-stores (:m ctx))]\\n        (when-not (contains? stores mid)\\n          (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :missing-module-store {:yin.k/hint mid}))\\n        (recur (assoc done mid (node :module-store [mid (store-node ctx (get stores mid))]))))\\n      (mapv val (sort-by #(str (key %)) done)))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- installing-names\\n  [m]\\n  (into #{} (mapcat (fn [[mn inst]]\\n                      (map #(symbol (name mn) (name %))\\n                           (get-in inst [:response :manifest :yin.module/exports]))))\\n        (:installs m)))\\n\\n\\n(defn live-pcs\\n  \\\"The pcs of v control flow can still reach from at: the successor\\n   relation (§8.1), so a backward jump makes earlier code live, and from\\n   each reachable :closure its body from the entry, since reachable code\\n   can still construct it.\\\"\\n  [v at]\\n  (loop [seen #{at}\\n         todo [at]]\\n    (if-let [p (peek todo)]\\n      (let [t (nth v p)\\n            fresh (remove seen (cond-> (analysis/successors v p)\\n                                 (= :closure (nth t 0)) (conj (nth t 3))))]\\n        (recur (into seen fresh) (into (pop todo) fresh)))\\n      seen)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- discharge!\\n  \\\"The dependency closure over the v4 vectors (§7.1), after the walk that\\n   found the contexts: every free occurrence control flow can still reach\\n   from a carried context (live-pcs) is answered there, in resolve-var's\\n   order: that context's\\n   E, then the one store engine/active-store selects for it (the root\\n   store, or the module store its store-of names; both travel), then a\\n   primitive, an installing module's export, the module registry. Else\\n   the lift is :yin.k/unsatisfied, discovery :incomplete.\\\"\\n  [ctx code]\\n  (let [m (:m ctx)\\n        installing (installing-names m)\\n        answered? (fn [sym e]\\n                    (let [store-of (engine/env-store-of e)\\n                          store (if (some? store-of) (get (:module-stores m) store-of {}) (:store m))]\\n                      (or (vm/reserved-name? sym) (contains? e sym) (contains? store sym)\\n                          (let [profile (vm/profile-of (:primitives m) sym)]\\n                            (when (= :host (:yin.k/class profile))\\n                              (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :host-state-primitive {:yin.k/name sym}))\\n                            (or (some? profile) (contains? installing sym)\\n                                (and (some? (namespace sym))\\n                                     (some? (module/resolve-module (:modules m)\\n                                                                   (symbol (str (namespace sym) \\\".\\\" (name sym)))))))))))\\n        scanned (into {} (map (fn [[a v]] [a (scan/free-occurrences v)])) code)\\n        missing (into #{}\\n                      (mapcat (fn [{:keys [a at env]}]\\n                                (let [live (live-pcs (get code a) at)]\\n                                  (keep (fn [o]\\n                                          (when (and (contains? live (:at o))\\n                                                     (not (answered? (:name o) env)))\\n                                            (:name o)))\\n                                        (get scanned a)))))\\n                      (:contexts @(:acc ctx)))]\\n    (when (seq missing)\\n      (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:yin.k/discovery :incomplete :yin.k/missing {:obligations missing}}))))\\n\\n\\n(declare lift-task*)\\n\\n\\n(defn- install-node\\n  [ctx mn inst opts]\\n  (let [{:keys [phase parent response]} inst\\n        response (into {} (remove (fn [[k _]]\\n                                    (and (keyword? k) (= \\\"yin.admit\\\" (namespace k)))))\\n                       response)]\\n    (when-not (contains? #{:running :parked} phase)\\n      (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :incomplete-install {:yin.k/name mn :yin.k/phase phase}))\\n    (when-not (try (cbor/encode response) true\\n                   (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _e false))\\n      (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :install-response {:yin.k/name mn}))\\n    (node :install [mn phase parent response\\n                    (lift-task* (:vm inst) (:serve! ctx)\\n                                (assoc (dissoc opts :free-env) :path (conj (:path ctx) mn)) :child)])))\\n\\n\\n(defn- lift-task*\\n  [m serve! opts role]\\n  (when (seq (:ready-queue m))\\n    (outcome! :yin.k/not-quiescent nil {:yin.k/ready (count (:ready-queue m))}))\\n  (when-some [h (unliftable-hold m)]\\n    (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :reason-mismatch {:yin.k/hold h}))\\n  (when (some? (:control m))\\n    (outcome! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint nil {:yin.k/pc (get-in m [:control :pc])}))\\n  (let [value (:value m)\\n        active? (and (map? value) (= :parked-continuation (:type value)) (contains? (:parked m) (:id value)))\\n        kind (cond active? :parked\\n                   (seq (:wait-set m)) :blocked\\n                   (engine/halted-with-empty-queue? m) :halted\\n                   :else (outcome! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint nil {}))\\n        ;; §6.3: the explicit argument overrides the kernel's retained field\\n        free-env (cond (some? (:free-env opts)) (:free-env opts)\\n                       (some? (:free-env m)) (:free-env m)\\n                       :else (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :missing-free-env {}))\\n        ctx {:m m :serve! serve! :serve-keyed (:serve-keyed opts) :path (or (:path opts) [])\\n             :acc (atom {:streams {} :cells {} :stores #{} :segments #{} :contexts #{}})}\\n        free-node (bindings-node ctx free-env)\\n        waits (mapv (fn [e] (node :wait [(state-node ctx e) (pending-node ctx e)])) (:wait-set m))\\n        parked (node :parked-table (mapcat (fn [[p rec]] [p (state-node ctx rec)]) (:parked m)))\\n        store (store-node ctx (:store m))\\n        result (when (= :halted kind) (lift-value ctx value))\\n        installs (mapv (fn [[mn inst]] (install-node ctx mn inst opts)) (sort-by #(str (key %)) (:installs m)))\\n        module-stores (module-store-nodes ctx)\\n        acc @(:acc ctx)\\n        segments (:segments acc)\\n        code (into {} (map (fn [a]\\n                             (if-some [v (get-in m [:code (get (:code-aliases m) a) :vector])]\\n                               [a v]\\n                               (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:yin.k/segment a}))))\\n                   segments)\\n        _ (discharge! ctx code)\\n        index (or (:source-index opts) {})\\n        missing-trees (into #{} (remove #(seq (get index %))) segments)\\n        _ (when (seq missing-trees)\\n            (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:yin.k/discovery :incomplete :yin.k/missing {:yin.k/trees missing-trees}}))\\n        requires {:yin.k/cursor-profiles (if (seq (:cells acc)) remote/cursor-profiles #{})\\n                  :yin.k/segments segments\\n                  :yin.k/trees (select-keys index segments)}\\n        task (node :task [3 profile kind role (or (:id-counter m) 0) free-node store module-stores parked\\n                          (node :cursor-cells (mapcat identity (:cells acc))) requires code installs waits\\n                          (when (= :parked kind) (:id value)) result nil])]\\n    ;; §3.3: a frame the evaluator itself minted that fails is inconsistent\\n    (when-let [d (validate-frames task)]\\n      (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :inconsistent-state {:yin.k/defect d}))\\n    task))\\n\\n\\n(declare task-tree)\\n\\n\\n(defn- header-custody\\n  \\\"The root's custody slot from the caller's header, by kind: blocked or\\n   parked takes the occurrence, arbitration, counter and the exclusive\\n   policy, and the origin when the header names one; halted the origin\\n   alone (an empty map without one, which the grammar refuses). A nil\\n   value is an absent key (handoff.cljc's header-of).\\\"\\n  [header kind]\\n  (into {}\\n        (filter (comp some? val))\\n        (if (= :halted kind)\\n          (select-keys header [:yin.k/origin])\\n          (assoc (select-keys header [:yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/next-op-seq :yin.k/origin])\\n                 :yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- protect!\\n  \\\"Every retained write of the tree under the header's enrolled set (UCF\\n   7.4.3, 7.7.8; handoff.cljc's protected!): an enrolled target without an\\n   operation id is :unprotected-pending, an id on an unenrolled target is\\n   :yin.k/unsatisfied naming the stream.\\\"\\n  [task enrolled]\\n  (doseq [[t _] (task-tree task :root)\\n          w (nth (:slots t) 13)]\\n    (let [ss (:slots (second (:slots w)))]\\n      (when-let [[ti _ oi] (get write-slots (first ss))]\\n        (let [identity (first (:slots (nth ss ti)))\\n    module/link-request-resource module/link-response-resource})\\n\\n\\n(defn- fresh-key!\\n  [used]\\n  (loop [n (inc (count @used))]\\n    (let [k (keyword \\\"yin.k\\\" (str \\\"k-\\\" n))]\\n      (if (contains? @used k) (recur (inc n)) (do (swap! used conj k) k)))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- rows-of\\n  \\\"Every row of kind under n; install children too unless own-only.\\\"\\n  [n kind own-only?]\\n  (let [out (atom [])]\\n    (letfn [(visit\\n              [n]\\n              (when (= kind (:kind n)) (swap! out conj n))\\n              (doseq [[d x] (map vector (descriptors (:kind n) (:slots n)) (:slots n))]\\n                (cond\\n                  (and (ref? d) (= :task (:kind x))) (when-not own-only? (visit x))\\n                  (ref? d) (visit x)\\n                  (refs? d) (run! visit x)\\n                  (and (value-slot? d) (vector? x) (= :row (first x))) (visit (second x))\\n                  :else nil)))]\\n      (visit n)\\n      @out)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- task-tree\\n  \\\"[task role] for the root and every install child, pre-order.\\\"\\n  [task role]\\n  (into [[task role]] (mapcat #(task-tree (nth (:slots %) 4) :child)) (nth (:slots task) 12)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- check-stores!\\n  \\\"Step 7's task context, beside X1: no root or module store key is a\\n   reserved name (Rule R), refused here rather than by restore's store-put.\\\"\\n  [_recv task _role]\\n  (let [[_ _ _ _ _ _ store module-stores] (:slots task)]\\n    (doseq [s (cons store (map #(second (:slots %)) module-stores))\\n            k (take-nth 2 (:slots s))]\\n      (when (vm/reserved-name? k)\\n        (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :reserved-name {:yin.k/role :store-key :yin.k/name k})))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- attaches?\\n  \\\"The receiving kernel admits vector v (its loader's validation), under\\n   address a when a is given.\\\"\\n  [recv v a]\\n  (try (let [r (module/attach-module recv v)] (or (nil? a) (contains? (:code-aliases r) a)))\\n       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _e false)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- check-install!\\n  \\\"One install record: a phase the engine holds a carried child in, the\\n   retained response link-install reads (status, manifest naming this\\n   module, exports) with the image spawn-child loads, the response's link\\n   id equal to the row's parent (the engine settles only the response of\\n   its own link), the image the manifest names (continuation §11 Q3: the\\n   manifest's :yin.semantic/code derivation record is the response's\\n   :derivation, from the manifest's tree to the image's A), and a child\\n   that is blocked: the engine links a halted child in the sweep it\\n   halts in.\\\"\\n  [recv inst]\\n  (let [[mn phase parent response child] (:slots inst)\\n        manifest (when (map? response) (:manifest response))\\n        child-kind (nth (:slots child) 2)]\\n    (when-not (contains? #{:running :parked} phase)\\n      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :install-phase {:yin.k/name mn :yin.k/phase phase}))\\n    (when-not (and (map? response) (= :ok (:status response)) (map? manifest)\\n                   (not-any? #(= \\\"yin.admit\\\" (namespace %)) (filter keyword? (keys response)))\\n                   (= mn (:yin.module/name manifest))\\n                   (coll? (:yin.module/exports manifest)) (every? symbol? (:yin.module/exports manifest))\\n                   (map? (:image response)) (attaches? recv (:value (:image response)) nil))\\n      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :install-response {:yin.k/name mn}))\\n    (when-not (and (some? parent) (= parent (:yin.link/id response)))\\n      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :install-link-id {:yin.k/name mn}))\\n    (let [record (:derivation response)]\\n      (when-not (and (map? record)\\n                     (jing/segment-matches? (get-in manifest [:yin.module/derivations :yin.semantic/code]) record)\\n                     (= (:yin.ledger/input record) (:yin.module/tree manifest))\\n                     (jing/segment-matches? (:yin.ledger/output record) (:value (:image response))))\\n        (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :install-image {:yin.k/name mn})))\\n    (when-not (= :blocked child-kind)\\n      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :install-child {:yin.k/name mn :yin.k/task-kind child-kind}))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- check-pendings!\\n  \\\"Step 8, pending and operations: role, kind, parked id, every :install\\n   pending names a carried install, every install record.\\\"\\n  [recv task role]\\n  (let [[_ _ kind role' _ _ _ _ parked _ _ _ installs waits parked-id] (:slots task)]\\n    (when-not (= role role') (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :role {:yin.k/role role'}))\\n    (let [names (into #{} (map #(first (:slots %))) installs)]\\n      (doseq [w waits]\\n        (let [[reason n] (:slots (second (:slots w)))]\\n          (when (and (= :install reason) (not (contains? names n)))\\n            (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :incomplete-install {:yin.k/name n})))))\\n    (case kind\\n      :halted (when (seq waits) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :kind {:yin.k/task-kind kind}))\\n      :blocked (when (empty? waits) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :kind {:yin.k/task-kind kind}))\\n      :parked (when-not (some #(= parked-id %) (take-nth 2 (:slots parked)))\\n                (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :parked-id {}))\\n      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :kind {:yin.k/task-kind kind}))\\n    (run! #(check-install! recv %) installs)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- check-install-admission!\\n  \\\"Carried children require the receiver composition's explicit name/address\\n   admission. Sender admission evidence never authorizes a receiver install.\\\"\\n  [task opts]\\n  (doseq [inst (nth (:slots task) 12)]\\n    (let [[mn _ _ response] (:slots inst)\\n          address (jing/segment-key (:manifest response))]\\n      (when-not (= address (get (:yin.k/admitted-modules opts) mn))\\n        (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil\\n                  {:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {mn address}}})))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- check-closure!\\n  \\\"A closure row names a :closure tuple of its carried vector: the entry\\n   (:closure-origin) and that tuple's binders (:closure-binders), as\\n   lower-closure will demand.\\\"\\n  [code c]\\n  (let [[a entry params] (:slots c)\\n        v (get code a)\\n        _ (when (nil? v) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :segment {:yin.k/segment a}))\\n        tuple (first (filter #(and (= :closure (nth % 0)) (= entry (nth % 3))) v))]\\n    (cond\\n      (nil? tuple) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :closure-origin {:yin.k/segment a :yin.k/entry entry})\\n      (not= params (nth tuple 2)) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :closure-binders {:yin.k/segment a :yin.k/entry entry})\\n      :else nil)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- check-dependencies!\\n  \\\"Step 9, dependency closure: requires and code agree, every segment has\\n   its trees (§6.1), every closure's and frame's store-of names a module\\n   store of this task (not a parent's or sibling's of the same key), every\\n   segment is a vector the receiver's kernel admits under its A, every\\n   closure names a closure of its code, every :prim is the receiver's.\\\"\\n  [recv task _role]\\n  (let [[_ _ _ _ _ _ _ module-stores _ _ requires code] (:slots task)]\\n    (when-not (and (map? requires) (= (set (:yin.k/segments requires)) (set (keys code))))\\n      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :requires {}))\\n    (let [trees (:yin.k/trees requires)\\n          missing (into #{} (remove #(seq (get trees %))) (keys code))]\\n      (when (seq missing)\\n        (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:yin.k/discovery :incomplete :yin.k/missing {:yin.k/trees missing}})))\\n    ;; §2.6: every store-of resolves to a module store this task carries\\n    (let [census (into #{} (map #(first (:slots %))) module-stores)\\n          missing (into #{} (comp (keep #(nth (:slots %) (if (= :closure (:kind %)) 4 1)))\\n                                  (remove census))\\n                        (concat (rows-of task :closure true) (rows-of task :env true)))]\\n      (when (seq missing)\\n        (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:yin.k/discovery :incomplete :yin.k/missing {:yin.k/stores missing}})))\\n    (doseq [[a v] (sort-by #(str (key %)) code)]\\n      (when-not (attaches? recv v a)\\n        (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :segment {:yin.k/segment a})))\\n    (run! #(check-closure! code %) (rows-of task :closure true))\\n    (doseq [p (rows-of task :prim true)]\\n      (when-not (contains? (:primitives recv) (first (:slots p)))\\n        (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:yin.k/name (first (:slots p))})))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- accept-grant!\\n  \\\"The grant checks of a blocked or parked exclusive root (handoff.cljc's\\n   accept-grant!, ported verbatim, keyed off the root's custody slot c and\\n   the carrier's pack address): evidence, binding, lease, holder,\\n   arbitration, epoch, tenure and the input prefix; then protection in both\\n   directions over every stream row of the tree, and op-id presence equal\\n   to enrollment on every retained write. Answers the custody state the\\n   restored root holds, its counter the slot's exactly.\\\"\\n  [task c address opts]\\n  (let [grant (:grant opts)\\n        evidence (:evidence grant)]\\n    (when-not (and (or (nil? grant) (map? grant))\\n                   (or (nil? evidence) (map? evidence)))\\n      (throw (ex-info \\\"Malformed lower grant or evidence\\\" {})))\\n    (when-not evidence\\n      (outcome! :yin.k/awaiting-grant nil {}))\\n    (when-not (= :yin.k/ready (:yin.k/status evidence))\\n      (outcome! (if (= :yin.k/awaiting-grant (:yin.k/status evidence))\\n                  :yin.k/awaiting-grant :yin.k/unsatisfied)\\n                nil (dissoc evidence :yin.k/status)))\\n    (let [binding (:yin.k/binding evidence)\\n          prefix (:yin.k/prefix evidence)\\n          tenure (:tenure grant)\\n          occurrence (:yin.k/occurrence c)\\n          lease (:dao.lease/lease grant)\\n          holder (:dao.lease/holder grant)\\n          frontier (:yin.k/frontier prefix)\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/1793600000000-engineer-module-pins-r2c.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:22:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_9\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"tail -65 collab/1793550000000-architect-module-pins-review.report.md; sed -n '990,1100p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; sed -n '2200,2320p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; sed -n '60,155p' src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc; sed -n '215,285p' src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"Verdict for Part A: **CHANGES-REQUIRED** (P1-1 blocking; P2-2 rename and the P2-1 ledger row land with it; P3-1/P3-2 deferred to round 2).\\n\\n## Part B: ruling on host-module (\\\"nil\\\") pins\\n\\n### B.0 Facts the ruling rests on\\n\\n- A host-registered entry has `:address nil` and lists its exports as `:yin.module/primitives {sym profile-address}` (`register-host-module`, `module.cljc:223-263`). `module/host-export-profile` answers exactly that profile address for a qualified symbol (`module.cljc:266-281`): a **keyword** `:yin.k.pp/blake3-…` minted by `vm/primitive-profile` over `{name class arities effects host-state}` (`vm.cljc:338-356`). Plain data, no functions, no host objects. The core `stream` and `cell` modules are host modules with literal cljc profiles and `:none` host-state (`module.cljc:350-363, 405-410`), so their addresses are identical on JVM, Node and Dart.\\n- The linker already defines \\\"satisfied by equal profile\\\" for exactly this case: `declared-discharge` discharges a primitive obligation by `(= profile (module/host-export-profile modules name))` (`linker.cljc:1014-1018`), and a module obligation by equal manifest address (`:1022-1027`). UCF §7.6.5 already carries `:yin.k/primitives {name <expected profile>}` in the outcome.\\n- The lift's `discharge!` answers a qualified free name by registry presence (`rows.cljc:1611-1616`) and nothing of the entry travels. The task row's `requires` slot is a plain map (`rows.cljc:1687-1689`), so two more keys cost no slot change.\\n\\n### B.1 Ruling\\n\\n1. **Host modules participate in this slice.** Not deferred. Reason: `stream` and `cell`, the most common modules in any pack, are host modules; deferring leaves R6 (silent skew) open for the common case while closing it only for DHT-linked modules. The data is already pure, the comparison already exists in the linker, and the lift already resolves the entry. The risk of implementing is one more `requires` key and a fixture re-mint, both owed anyway for `:yin.k/modules`. The risk of deferring is a second re-mint later and a documented hole in the fetch-loop contract.\\n\\n2. **What the lift records.** Only what the live code uses: for every live free name `ns/f` that `discharge!` answered through the registry (`rows.cljc:1614-1616`, after `E`, store, primitives and installing names, which stay as they are):\\n   - `:yin.k/modules` gets `{ns <manifest address>}` when the entry is linked (`(:address entry)` non-nil), `{ns nil}` when it is host-registered;\\n   - `:yin.k/host-exports` gets `{ns/f <profile address>}` when the entry is host-registered, the value being `(module/host-export-profile (:modules m) 'ns/f)`.\\n   Not all exports. Recording all exports would refuse a receiver whose host module gained or changed an export the code never touches, and it would persist what the free-name scan already derives. A lift where `host-export-profile` answers nil for a name the registry claims to hold (an entry with a malformed `:yin.module/primitives`) is `:yin.k/non-portable :host-export-profile {:yin.k/name ns/f}`.\\n\\n3. **Canonical encoding.** Two maps in the task row's `requires` beside `:yin.k/segments`, `:yin.k/trees` and `:yin.k/cursor-profiles`: `:yin.k/modules {symbol -> string-or-nil}` and `:yin.k/host-exports {qualified-symbol -> keyword}`. Keys sorted by the carrier's existing rules for symbol keys; the `keyed`/`built` host-collapse discipline applies (module names contain dots, no slash; a qualified export has one slash, so the known P3 `keyed` gap does not reach these maps, but add the count guard anyway as the `built` precedent). Absent maps are not emitted when empty (same as `:yin.k/trees` with no segments is still emitted; follow whatever the existing `requires` does for empties, byte-stable). No richer value in `:yin.k/modules`: a tagged vector `[:host profiles]` beside address strings mixes value kinds in one slot and duplicates the primitives precedent for no gain.\\n\\n4. **How the lower compares** (new `check-modules!`, one pass over the whole tree, after `check-custody!`, before `attach-streams!`, absorbing today's `check-install-admission!`):\\n   - `:yin.k/modules {ns address}`: receiver's `module/resolve-module` entry exists with `(= address (:address entry))` → satisfied. Entry exists with another address (including a host entry, nil, where a linked one was pinned, or vice versa) → **terminal** `{:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied :yin.k/kind :module-pin-mismatch :yin.k/name ns :yin.k/pinned address :yin.k/linked (:address entry)}`, the `:dependency-pin-mismatch` words (`engine.cljc:1388-1393`). Entry absent → collected into `:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {ns address}}`.\\n   - `:yin.k/host-exports {ns/f profile}`: `(= profile (module/host-export-profile (:modules recv) 'ns/f))` → satisfied. Receiver answers another profile → **terminal** `{:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied :yin.k/kind :host-export-mismatch :yin.k/name ns/f :yin.k/pinned profile :yin.k/held <receiver's>}`. Receiver answers nil (no such export, or the module is absent, or it is linked rather than host) → collected into `:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/host-exports {ns/f profile}}` (the `:yin.k/modules {ns nil}` entry will be in the same map when the module is absent).\\n   - Receiver's host module exporting **more** than the pin names: satisfied (subset by construction, since only used exports are pinned). Equality is of profile addresses, never of normalised profile maps: the address already covers name, class, arities, effects and host-state.\\n   - Carried install children: `:yin.k/admitted-modules {ns address}` equality as today; unlisted → collected into `:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {ns carried-address}}`.\\n   - Order: terminal mismatches are thrown first (nothing the composition can fetch repairs them), then one collected refusal `{:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied :yin.k/discovery :complete :yin.k/missing {…}}` with keys present only where something is missing. Zero attaches in every case.\\n   - The fetch loop (composition, not this slice) requires only keys of `:yin.k/missing :yin.k/modules` whose pin is non-nil; a nil pin and every `:yin.k/host-exports` entry are composition prerequisites and are not fetched.\\n\\n5. **Determinism across hosts.** Profile addresses are BLAKE3 content hashes over plain data computed identically on all three hosts (the same mechanism Stage E already pins for primitives); manifest addresses are segment keys. The refusal maps are plain data. Pin T8 in `stage_e_rows_test.cljc`: a `requires` with both maps re-encodes byte-identically and the two terminal refusals and the collected refusal are `=` across JVM, Node and Dart.\\n\\n6. **Threat-model text amended by this ruling.** §4.2's shape gains `:yin.k/host-exports`; \\\"whose export profiles equal those the lift recorded\\\" becomes \\\"whose profile address for each used export equals the pinned one\\\"; §4.4's option is renamed `:yin.k/admitted-modules` and its refusal is folded into the collected shape with `:yin.k/discovery :complete`. T4 reads: a nil pin plus `:yin.k/host-exports` is satisfied by a host module answering equal profile addresses for the pinned exports; another profile for a pinned export refuses `:host-export-mismatch`; a missing export is collected as missing; extra exports are ignored.\\n\\n### B.2 Alternative considered and rejected\\n\\n\\\"Refuse nothing for nil pins, document, defer\\\": `:yin.k/modules {ns nil}` would then only assert \\\"a host module of this name must exist\\\", which `resolve-var` already enforces at run time, and skew in `stream`/`cell` profiles between two compositions would still run under R's authority (R6, R8 for the common case). The saving is one map and one lift line; not worth a second re-mint. Rejected.\\n\\n## Part C: ordered steps for codex round 2\\n\\nPreconditions: worktree `datomworld-srvm-pins`, the current 13 files uncommitted. `npm ci` and `mise trust` are done there. Per-iteration verification is `bb test:clj`; full three-host `bb test` once at the end, one lane set at a time, foreground only. Read `docs/agents/build-n-test.md` first. No `collab/` path is ever staged.\\n\\n**Commit 1 (R4, lands alone): fix P1-1, rename P2-2, ledger P2-1.**\\n1. `rows.cljc` `install-node`: `response` → `(dissoc response :yin.admit/id :yin.admit/decision :yin.admit/asserters :yin.admit/address)` before the `cbor/encode` check and the row. Delete the restore-side `dissoc` (`rows.cljc:2233-2237` and its comment).\\n2. `rows.cljc` `check-install!`: add to the existing `and` of the `:install-response` clause `(not-any? #(= \\\"yin.admit\\\" (namespace %)) (filter keyword? (keys response)))`.\\n3. Rename `:yin.k/admitted` → `:yin.k/admitted-modules` in `rows.cljc`, `export.cljc`, `rows_support.cljc`, `rows_test.cljc`, `rows_custody_test.cljc`, `export_test.cljc`, `safepoint_harness_test.cljc`.\\n4. Tests in `rows_test.cljc` `carried-install-requires-receiver-admission`: keep every assertion; add (a) the decoded wire's root `:install` row slot 3 has none of the four keys, (b) the harness-style relift of the lowered machine is `=` by root to the wire (reuse `canonical-under` or compare the install row), (c) a pack with the four keys spliced into the install row refuses `:yin.k/undecodable :install-response` with zero attaches. In `export_test.cljc`: a frozen parked-installer whose source response carried the sender record rehydrates `:ok` and reproduces the pack byte for byte (this is the P1-1 regression pin).\\n5. Mutants (run, record counts, restore): (m1) lift keeps the sender keys → 4(a), 4(b)/export pin fail; (m2) `check-install!` accepts `:yin.admit/*` keys → 4(c) fails; (m3) gate bypass → as before.\\n6. Docs (P3-3 list): reword \\\"dropped on restore\\\" to \\\"never carried by the lift; a carried one is refused\\\", rename the option, add the known-gaps row for P2-1 (holder driver seam, P2) and the P3-2 docstring note. Revisions I-8 wording likewise.\\n7. `bb test:clj`, kondo on changed files, `git diff --check`. Report; Architect sign-off; commit `fix(yin.vm.ucf): carried install children need receiver admission; lift never carries sender admission` (format.md convention, no Co-Authored-By).\\n\\n**Commit 2 (pins carrier + lift + lower + driver seam): the ruling.**\\n8. `rows.cljc` lift: in `discharge!` (or a sibling collector over the same `answered?` walk), record for every live registry-answered name the entry: linked → `:yin.k/modules {ns address}`; host → `:yin.k/modules {ns nil}` and `:yin.k/host-exports {ns/f profile}`; nil profile → `:yin.k/non-portable :host-export-profile`. Put both maps into `requires` (`rows.cljc:1687-1689`), sorted, empty maps handled as the existing `requires` keys handle empties.\\n9. Encoder/decoder/validator: `requires` is a plain map today, so confirm `check-dependencies!` (`rows.cljc:1918`) still accepts the two extra keys and add the key-count guard for symbol keys as in `built`. Malformed-slot collection: non-map `:yin.k/modules`, non-symbol key, non-string-non-nil value, non-keyword `:yin.k/host-exports` value, unqualified `:yin.k/host-exports` key → `:yin.k/undecodable :requires` (extend the existing kind, no new kind).\\n10. `rows.cljc` lower: replace `check-install-admission!` by `check-modules!` per B.1 item 4 (terminal mismatches first, then one collected refusal with `:yin.k/discovery :complete`, zero attaches), same position (after custody, before attach). Delete `check-install-admission!`.\\n11. Driver seam (P2-1): `driver/lowered` and the fenced recovery call forward `(:yin.k/admitted-modules (:config state))`; `rehydrate-fenced` already forwards. One driver test with and without the config over a parked-installer checkpoint.\\n12. Tests (threat model §7.1, amended): T1 (lift of harness row 17 emits `{:yin.k/modules {host.mod nil} :yin.k/host-exports {host.mod/f <profile>}}`; a DHT-linked fixture emits `{pym.k <address>}`; names answered by `E`, store, prims or module stores emit nothing), T2 (receiver lacking the module: collected refusal, `:discovery :complete`, zero attaches), T3 (linked module at another address: `:module-pin-mismatch` naming both; equal address lowers), T4 (B.1 item 6), T5 (already in commit 1, re-point to the collected shape), T8 (Stage E cross-host row), T9 (layering: `rows.cljc` requires neither `linker.interpreter`, `linker.dht` nor `dao.lease`), T10 (`resolve-var` unchanged). T6/T7 (fetch loop, lease) are composition work, out of this slice; leave their known-gaps rows.\\n13. Mutants (run, record, restore): lift records all exports instead of used; lower compares by name presence instead of address; lower accepts a different profile address; lower reports `:incomplete`; attach before `check-modules!`. Each must be killed by a named test.\\n14. Fixture re-mint: `rows-checkpoint-v3.txt` and any ledger/Stage E fixture whose `requires` now carries the two maps; record old → new addresses in the report and in `yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md` (I-8 completes, dated). C4 scanner pins are untouched (AST-level; see the standing note).\\n15. Docs: continuation §2.5 (binding fact travels: the two maps), §7.1 step 6 (records address or host profile), §7.2 dependencies row (module check, three refusal kinds, delete \\\"the lower does not re-discharge\\\"), §11 Q5 closed as C with the host-export ruling, Q3 (admitted set is `:yin.k/admitted-modules`); UCF §7.6.4 (add the host-export sentence), §7.6.5 (add `:yin.k/host-exports` to the outcome), §7.11 row updated; transport grammar (`requires` slot: the two maps); `yin.vm.linker.dht.md` 7.5.11 amendment reworded; threat-model report is a collab artifact, not edited; known-gaps: Q5 row → landed, R4 row → landed, P2-1 row → closed by step 11.\\n16. `bb test:clj` per iteration; at the end `bb test` all three hosts (foreground, one lane set at a time; \\\"Testing <ns>\\\" must appear in Node output); kondo; `git diff --check`. Report with counts, mutant kills, old → new addresses. Architect sign-off, then commit `feat(yin.vm.ucf): module pins and host-export pins in requires; lower re-discharges by equal address and profile` and, if the driver seam is separable, a third commit `feat(yin.vm.ucf.holder): admitted-modules config forwarded to the lower`.\\n\\nCommit split summary: (1) R4 alone, after the P1-1 fix and the rename; (2) carrier + lift + lower + tests + re-mint + docs; (3) optional driver seam if it would otherwise delay (2).\\n\\nCHANGES-REQUIRED (Part A)\\nRULING-READY\\n                  (let [id (first slots)]\\n                    (when-not (contains? correspondence id) (bad! :missing-stream-correspondence [id]))\\n                    (node :stream [(get correspondence id) (get correspondence id)]))\\n                  (node kind (mapv rewrite-slot (descriptors kind slots) slots)))))]\\n      (emit (rewrite task)))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- value-node\\n  [x]\\n  (check-literal-markers! x)\\n  [:lit x])\\n\\n\\n(defn- decoded-value\\n  [v]\\n  (case (first v)\\n    :row {:yin.k/row (second v)}\\n    :cursor-cell {:yin.k/cursor-cell (second v)}\\n    :lit (if (marker-shaped? (second v)) (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :marker []) (second v))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- keyed-node\\n  [kind m encode]\\n  (node kind (mapcat (fn [[k v]] [k (encode v)]) m)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- env-node\\n  [e encode]\\n  (node :env [(keyed-node :bindings (:yin.k/bindings e) encode) (:yin.k/store-of e)]))\\n\\n\\n(defn- kframe-node\\n  [f encode]\\n  (node :kframe [(:yin.k/segment f) (:yin.k/pc f) (env-node (:yin.k/env f) encode)\\n                 (keyed-node :window (:yin.k/window f) encode) (:yin.k/rd f)]))\\n\\n\\n(def pending-keys\\n  {:next [:yin.k/cursor-cell]\\n   :put [:yin.k/stream :yin.k/value :yin.k/op-id]\\n   :ffi [:yin.k/cursor-cell :yin.k/call-id :yin.k/op]\\n   :ffi-request [:yin.k/call-id :yin.k/envelope :yin.k/request-stream :yin.k/response-stream :yin.k/response-cursor-cell :yin.k/op-id]\\n   :link-request [:yin.k/link-id :yin.k/name :yin.k/request-stream :yin.k/response-stream :yin.k/cursor-cell :yin.k/envelope :yin.k/op-id :yin.k/try?]\\n   :link-response [:yin.k/link-id :yin.k/name :yin.k/request-stream :yin.k/response-stream :yin.k/cursor-cell :yin.k/try?]\\n   :install [:yin.k/name :yin.k/try?]})\\n\\n\\n(defn frame->rows\\n  \\\"Encode a keyed frame to a frame-rooted version-3 row pack. Values are\\n   plain literals by default. An explicit value encoder classifies portable\\n   references as [:row abstract-row] or [:cursor-cell id], distinct from guest maps.\\n   This reshapes; frame/defect owns semantic validity.\\\"\\n  ([f] (frame->rows f value-node))\\n  ([f encode]\\n   (let [k (node :k (mapv #(kframe-node % encode) (:yin.k/k f)))\\n         state (if (= :act (:yin.k/state f))\\n                 (node :act [(:yin.k/segment f) (:yin.k/pc f) (env-node (:yin.k/env f) encode)\\n                             (keyed-node :window (:yin.k/window f) encode) k (get-in f [:yin.k/deliver :yin.k/rd])])\\n                 (node :tail [(:yin.k/segment f) (:yin.k/site f) k]))\\n         pending (:yin.k/pending f)\\n         reason (:yin.k/reason pending)\\n         root (if (contains? f :yin.k/pending)\\n                (node :wait [state (node :pending\\n                                         (into [reason]\\n                                               (map (fn [key d]\\n                                                      (let [x (get pending key)]\\n                                                        (if (= :V d) (encode x) x)))\\n                                                    (get pending-keys reason) (get pending-table reason))))])\\n                state)\\n         [id rows] (emit-node root {} {})]\\n     (pack id rows))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- decode-keyed\\n  [n decode-value]\\n  (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k (decode-value v)])) (partition 2 (:slots n))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- decode-env\\n  [n decode-value]\\n  (let [[bindings store-of] (:slots n)]\\n    (cond-> {:yin.k/bindings (decode-keyed bindings decode-value)}\\n      (some? store-of) (assoc :yin.k/store-of store-of))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- decode-kframe\\n  [n decode-value]\\n  (let [[seg pc e w rd] (:slots n)]\\n    {:yin.k/frame-type :return :yin.k/segment seg :yin.k/pc pc\\n     :yin.k/env (decode-env e decode-value) :yin.k/window (decode-keyed w decode-value) :yin.k/rd rd}))\\n\\n\\n(defn- decode-frame\\n  [n decode-value]\\n  (if (= :wait (:kind n))\\n    (let [[state pending] (:slots n) [reason & slots] (:slots pending)]\\n      (assoc (decode-frame state decode-value) :yin.k/pending\\n             (into {:yin.k/reason reason}\\n                   (map (fn [key d x] [key (if (= :V d) (decode-value x) x)])\\n                        (get pending-keys reason) (get pending-table reason) slots))))\\n    (let [act? (= :act (:kind n)) [seg pc e w k rd] (:slots n)\\n          k (if act? k e)]\\n      (cond-> {:yin.k/state (:kind n) :yin.k/segment seg\\n               :yin.k/deliver (if act? {:yin.k/deliver :rd :yin.k/rd rd} {:yin.k/deliver :return})\\n               :yin.k/k (mapv #(decode-kframe % decode-value) (:slots k))}\\n        act? (assoc :yin.k/pc pc :yin.k/env (decode-env e decode-value) :yin.k/window (decode-keyed w decode-value))\\n        (not act?) (assoc :yin.k/site pc)))))\\n\\n\\n(defn rows->frame\\n  \\\"Validate row syntax and hashes, then reshape to the keyed frame.\\n                (case reason\\n                  :next (assoc p :reason :next :stream-id (cell-stream (first xs))\\n                               :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref :id (get cell-keys (first xs))})\\n                  :ffi (let [[c call-id op] xs]\\n                         (cond-> (assoc p :reason :next :stream-id (cell-stream c) :call-id call-id\\n                                        :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref :id (get cell-keys c)})\\n                           (some? op) (assoc :op op)))\\n                  :put (let [[s v op-id] xs]\\n                         (cond-> (assoc p :reason :put :stream-id (stream-key s) :datom (value v))\\n                           (some? op-id) (assoc :op-id op-id)))\\n                  :ffi-request (let [[call-id envelope req resp c op-id] xs\\n                                     datom (value envelope)]\\n                                 (cond-> (assoc p :reason :put :stream-id (stream-key req) :datom datom\\n                                                :request-sent true :call-id call-id :op (apply2/request-op datom)\\n                                                :response-cursor (get cell-keys c) :response-stream (stream-key resp))\\n                                   (some? op-id) (assoc :op-id op-id)))\\n                  (:link-request :link-response)\\n                  (let [[link-id mn _ _ c] xs\\n                        [envelope op-id] (when (= :link-request reason) (drop 5 xs))]\\n                    (cond-> (assoc p :reason reason :link-id link-id :name mn\\n                                   :request module/link-request-resource :response module/link-response-resource\\n                                   :try? (last xs) :cursor (second (:slots (get bodies c))))\\n                      (= :link-request reason) (assoc :envelope envelope)\\n                      (some? op-id) (assoc :op-id op-id)))\\n                  :install (assoc p :reason :install :name (first xs) :try? (second xs)))))]\\n      (let [store' (reduce (fn [s [k v]] (engine/store-put s k (value v))) {} (partition 2 (:slots store)))\\n            stores (into {} (map (fn [ms]\\n                                   (let [[mid s] (:slots ms)]\\n                                     [mid (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k (value v)])) (partition 2 (:slots s)))])))\\n                         module-stores)\\n            parked' (into {} (map (fn [[p _]] [p (parked-record p)])) parked-index)\\n            entries (mapv entry waits)\\n            link (some #(let [[reason _ _ req resp] (:slots (second (:slots %)))]\\n                          (when (contains? #{:link-request :link-response} reason) [req resp]))\\n                       waits)\\n            [base installs'] (reduce (fn [[r acc] inst]\\n                                       (let [[mn phase parent response child] (:slots inst)\\n                                             [spawned r'] (spawn-child r response mn (:fenced? custody))]\\n                                         [r' (assoc acc mn {:phase phase :parent parent :response response\\n                                                            :vm (restore-task spawned child handles custody false)})]))\\n                                     [base {}] installs)\\n            fe (keyed free-env)\\n            resources (merge (:resources base)\\n                             (into {} (map (fn [[identity k]] [k (get handles identity)])) stream-keys)\\n                             (into {} (map (fn [[c body]]\\n                                             [(get cell-keys c) {:stream-id (stream-key (first (:slots body)))\\n                                                                 :cursor (second (:slots body))}]))\\n                                   pairs)\\n                             (when-let [[req resp] link]\\n                               {module/link-request-resource (get handles (first (:slots req)))\\n                                module/link-response-resource (get handles (first (:slots resp)))}))\\n            ;; a fenced rehydration carries the counter exactly, so the\\n            ;; relift reproduces the published root; a resumption adopts\\n            ;; max(local, carried)\\n            machine (cond-> (assoc base :store store' :module-stores stores :parked parked' :installs installs'\\n                                   :resources resources :env fe :free-env fe :window {} :k nil :control nil\\n                                   :ready-queue []\\n                                   :id-counter (if (:fenced? custody)\\n                                                 id-counter\\n                                                 (max (or (:id-counter base) 0) id-counter)))\\n                      ;; resource key -> the carrier's cursor cell, so one\\n                      ;; cell is one key and two cells two (UCF 7.7.4)\\n                      (:fenced? custody)\\n                      (assoc :yin.k/recovery-cell-ids (into {} (map (fn [[c k]] [k c])) cell-keys)))]\\n        (with-custody\\n          (case kind\\n            :halted (assoc machine :halted? true :blocked? false :value (value result) :wait-set [])\\n            :parked (assoc machine :halted? true :blocked? false :value (get parked' parked-id) :wait-set entries)\\n            (assoc machine :halted? false :blocked? true :value :yin/blocked :wait-set entries))\\n          custody kind root?)))))\\n\\n\\n(defn lower-task\\n  \\\"The lower of §7.2 into recv, a fresh semantic machine of the\\n   receiver's composition: gate to frames (decode) and the store keys,\\n   then pendings and install records, dependency closure (code, closures,\\n   primitives), each step over the whole tree before the next, then\\n   custody (check-custody!), all before the first attach! (step 11); then\\n   restore (step 12), which therefore meets no carrier defect. Answers the\\n   restored machine, or throws the first refusal as ex-data.\\n   opts: :budget; :yin.k/admitted-modules, a composition-supplied {name manifest-address}\\n   for carried install children (default empty, fail closed);\\n   :exclusive, refuse a fork root; :grant and :protection,\\n   required by a blocked or parked exclusive root (handoff.cljc's reader\\n   contract: the grant names :checkpoint, the pack address, its lease,\\n   holder, tenure and evidence; :protection maps every stream identity of\\n   the tree to its class); :fenced, an administrative rehydration that\\n   skips the grant and restores every task of the tree gated :exporting,\\n   its waits in :yin.k/recovery-waits and its parked records in\\n   :yin.k/recovery-parked (none in the scheduler), its id counter the\\n   carried one exactly and :yin.k/recovery-cell-ids mapping each cursor\\n   cell's resource key to its carried cell id.\\n   Name-keyed admission is flat over the whole task tree: the same name at\\n   different addresses cannot be admitted together. The lift never carries\\n   sender admission fields; a carried one is refused as\\n   :yin.k/undecodable :install-response.\\\"\\n  ([recv wire attach!] (lower-task recv wire attach! {}))\\n  ([recv wire attach! opts]\\n   (let [task (decode wire (merge default-budget (:budget opts)))]\\n     (when-not (= :task (:kind task)) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :root {}))\\n     ;; each step over the whole tree before the next (§3.3)\\n     (doseq [step [check-stores! check-pendings! check-dependencies!]\\n             [t role] (task-tree task :root)]\\n       (step recv t role))\\n     (let [custody (check-custody! task wire opts)]\\n       (doseq [[t _] (task-tree task :root)]\\n         (check-install-admission! t opts))\\n       (restore-task recv task (attach-streams! attach! task) custody true)))))\\n  \\\"The registry entry of module `module-name` in `modules` (a registry's\\n   `:modules` map), or nil when the dotted path reaches no module entry.\\\"\\n  [modules module-name]\\n  (let [node (reduce (fn [node seg] (when (map? node) (get node seg)))\\n                     modules\\n                     (symbol->path module-name))]\\n    (when (and (map? node) (contains? node :manifest)) node)))\\n\\n\\n(defn assoc-module\\n  \\\"Return registry with `entry` installed as module `module-name`.\\\"\\n  [registry module-name entry]\\n  (assoc-in (or registry (empty-registry))\\n            (into [:modules] (symbol->path module-name))\\n            entry))\\n\\n\\n(defn link-module\\n  \\\"The `linked` transition's registry update (yin.vm.linker.md sections\\n   7.3 and 8.3): `registry` gains the module `manifest` names as the\\n   portable encoding of acts 1 to 3 -- `{:manifest m :address a\\n   :derivation d :slice {sym encoded} :stores {address snapshot} :cells\\n   {cell-id cell} :images {identity image}}` -- never lowered values. `a`\\n   is the manifest's own address; `lifted` is the act-1 lift, `{:slice\\n   :stores :cells :images}`, the cells being the logical cursor cells its\\n   references name (r9) and the images the verified origin images a\\n   receiving task attaches.\\n   Each receiving task lowers the entry into its own `:bindings`.\\\"\\n  [registry manifest derivation lifted]\\n  (assoc-module registry\\n                (:yin.module/name manifest)\\n                {:manifest manifest,\\n                 :address (jing/segment-key manifest),\\n                 :derivation derivation,\\n                 :slice (:slice lifted),\\n                 :stores (:stores lifted),\\n                 :cells (:cells lifted),\\n                 :images (:images lifted)}))\\n\\n\\n(defn module-entries\\n  \\\"Every `[name entry]` a registry value holds, the module name read back\\n   from each entry's manifest.\\\"\\n  [registry]\\n  (letfn [(walk\\n            [node]\\n            (when (map? node)\\n              (if (contains? node :manifest)\\n                [[(:yin.module/name (:manifest node)) node]]\\n                (mapcat walk (vals node)))))]\\n    (vec (walk (:modules registry)))))\\n\\n\\n(defn pin-conflict\\n  \\\"The deterministic refusal when receiving `entry` as `module-name`\\n   would disagree with a linked manifest's dependency pin. Missing\\n   dependencies are permitted; pins are derived from registry manifests.\\\"\\n  [registry module-name entry]\\n  (let [linked (filter (fn [[_ e]] (some? (:address e)))\\n                       (module-entries registry))\\n        existing (keep (fn [[owner e]]\\n                         (let [requires (:yin.module/requires (:manifest e))]\\n                           (when (and (contains? requires module-name)\\n                                      (not= (get requires module-name)\\n                                            (:address entry)))\\n                             [module-name owner (get requires module-name)\\n                              (:address entry)])))\\n                       linked)\\n        incoming (keep (fn [[name pinned]]\\n                         (when-let [held (module-entry (:modules registry) name)]\\n                           (when (not= pinned (:address held))\\n                             [name module-name pinned (:address held)])))\\n                       (:yin.module/requires (:manifest entry)))\\n        conflict (first (sort-by (fn [[name owner pinned address]]\\n                                   [(str name) (str owner) (str pinned) (str address)])\\n                                 (concat existing incoming)))]\\n    (when-let [[name _ pinned address] conflict]\\n      {:status :refused,\\n       :reason :dependency-pin-mismatch,\\n       :module module-name,\\n       :name name,\\n       :pinned pinned,\\n       :linked address})))\\n\\n\\n(defn resolve-module\\n  \\\"Get a value from a registry value by dotted symbol path.\\n   (resolve-module r 'io)                    → the 'io registry entry\\n   (resolve-module r 'io.file-output-stream) → the specific export\\\"\\n  [registry sym]\\n  (walk-path (:modules registry) (symbol->path sym)))\\n\\n\\n(defn register-effect-handler\\n  \\\"Return registry with handler-fn installed for effect keyword kw.\\n   Handler: (fn [state effect opts] -> {:state s :value v :blocked? bool})\\\"\\n  [module-name sym profile]\\n  (when-let [rule (if (nil? profile)\\n                    :missing-profile\\n                    (profile-rule profile))]\\n    (throw (ex-info \\\"Host module registration refused\\\"\\n                    {:rule rule, :module module-name, :name sym}))))\\n\\n\\n(defn register-host-module\\n  \\\"Return registry with host module `module-name` installed from `fns`\\n   under `profiles`.\\n\\n   module-name is a dotted symbol; fns maps each export symbol to the host\\n   value it publishes; profiles maps each export symbol to its UCF 7.5.2\\n   profile record in the shape of `yin.vm/primitive-profiles`. Every\\n   binding must carry a profile, and the profile's class must be `:pure`,\\n   or `:effectful` with a declared, non-empty `:yin.k/effects` set, with\\n   `:yin.k/host-state` `:none`. An `:effectful` export returns an\\n   effect minted by `make-effect` for the engine to interpret and\\n   performs no IO itself; `stream/make` is exactly such a constructor.\\n   Each export's declared effect set is also entered in the registry's\\n   identity-keyed `:callable-effects`, which the engine checks an\\n   effect's kind against (D4).\\n\\n   The module is entered as an already-linked manifest with\\n   `:yin.module/tree` absent, `:yin.module/derivations {}`, and its\\n   exports listed under `:yin.module/primitives` by profile address; the\\n   exports themselves are its `:slice`, and its `:address` and\\n   `:derivation` are nil because no content was fetched or derived: the\\n   host is the boundary.\\\"\\n  [registry module-name fns profiles]\\n  (doseq [sym (sort-by str (keys fns))]\\n    (check-binding! module-name sym (get profiles sym)))\\n  (-> (or registry (empty-registry))\\n      (update :callable-effects\\n              (partial merge-with into)\\n              (vm/callable-effects fns profiles))\\n      (assoc-in (into [:modules] (symbol->path module-name))\\n                {:manifest {:yin.module/name module-name,\\n                            :yin.module/derivations {},\\n                            :yin.module/primitives\\n                            (into {} (map (fn [[sym _f]]\\n                                            [sym (:yin.k/profile\\n                                                   (get profiles sym))]))\\n                                  fns)},\\n                 :address nil,\\n                 :derivation nil,\\n                 :slice fns,\\n                 :stores {}})))\\n\\n\\n(defn host-export-profile\\n  \\\"The profile address host module `ns` publishes for export `name`, when\\n   `qualified-sym` is `ns/name` and `registry` holds `ns` as a\\n   host-registered entry (`register-host-module`'s shape, `:address`\\n   nil); else nil. A linked entry never answers: the\\n   `:yin.module/primitives` of a fetched manifest are the primitives that\\n   module assumes, not exports it provides.\\\"\\n  [registry qualified-sym]\\n  (when (and (symbol? qualified-sym) (some? (namespace qualified-sym)))\\n    (let [entry (module-entry (:modules registry)\\n                              (symbol (namespace qualified-sym)))]\\n      (when (and (some? entry) (nil? (:address entry)))\\n        (get-in entry [:manifest :yin.module/primitives\\n                       (symbol (name qualified-sym))])))))\\n\\n\\n;; =============================================================================\\n;; Effect descriptors\\n;; =============================================================================\\n\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/1793600000000-engineer-module-pins-r2c.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:24:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_10\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n 'registry|host.mod|requires|malformed|module-pin' test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc; cat test/yin/vm/ucf/stage_e_rows_test.cljc\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"16:            [yin.vm.malformed-rows :as malformed]))\\n1114:           [:install-child (support/parked-installer) [:installs 'host.mod :vm] 42]]]\\n1169:            \\\"the composition's registry is the receiver's\\\")\\n1250:        (doseq [path [[] [:installs 'host.mod :vm]]]\\n1284:        (is (= #{'c 'd} (set (keys (get-in recv [:module-stores 'host.mod])))))))))\\n1303:          pending [{:yin.k/reason :link-request :yin.k/link-id [:t0 7] :yin.k/name 'host.mod\\n1308:                   {:yin.k/reason :link-response :yin.k/link-id [:t0 7] :yin.k/name 'host.mod\\n1312:                   {:yin.k/reason :install :yin.k/name 'host.mod}]]\\n1344:(deftest malformed-ucf-rows-refuse-the-published-rule\\n1345:  (doseq [[label [expected wire]] malformed/malformed-ucf-row-sets]\\n1370:(deftest carried-install-requires-receiver-admission\\n1377:                          [:installs 'host.mod :response] merge sender-record)\\n1392:                  {:yin.k/admitted-modules {'host.mod :wrong-address}}\\n1393:                  {:yin.k/admitted-modules {'host.mod nil}}]]\\n1397:        (is (= {:yin.k/modules {'host.mod address}} (:yin.k/missing refusal)))\\n1400:          restored (rows/lower-task (assoc recv :attach-stream attach!) wire attach! {:yin.k/admitted-modules {'host.mod address}})\\n1401:          response (get-in restored [:installs 'host.mod :response])\\n1402:          child (get-in restored [:installs 'host.mod :vm])\\n1410:            installed (module/module-entry (:modules (:modules done)) 'host.mod)]\\n(ns yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-rows-test\\n  \\\"M-next stage E, the isolated-runtime form on every lane: every\\n   scenario of yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-scenarios run in this process, each\\n   life a fresh runtime over the scenario's durable root, each kill the\\n   life's mortal media going dead at its named cut.  On Dart this is the\\n   whole of stage E's evidence (its process transport is recorded\\n   separately); on the JVM and Node it is the same-runtime control\\n   beside the separate-process matrix of\\n   yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-process-test.\\n\\n   Full 13-row acceptance matrix mapping (linker-dht 14.2.4 & UCF 7.11):\\n   - Row 1: candidates and encodings (row-1-candidates-and-encodings-test)\\n   - Row 2: export phases & carrier failures (row-2-export-phases-test, row-2-carrier-failures-test)\\n   - Row 3: reclaim (row-3-reclaim-test)\\n   - Row 4: kills around result delivery (row-4-kills-around-result-delivery-test)\\n   - Row 5: replay divergence (row-5-replay-divergence-test)\\n   - Row 6: partition (row-6-partition-test)\\n   - Row 7: kills around completion & failure-lower (row-7-kills-around-completion-test, row-7-failure-lower-and-lost-authority-test)\\n   - Clause 8: admission order & cross-target conflict (clause-8-admission-order-test)\\n   - Clause 3: sequence and regrant (clause-3-sequence-and-regrant-test)\\n   - Fork: fork per host (fork-per-host-test)\\n   - Inbox & Journal: positional inboxes & crash recovery (inbox-and-journal-cuts-test)\\n   - Row 10 canonical-byte agreement: exercised cross-host in stage-e-process-test\\n     (ordered JVM/Node pairs over file media).\\\"\\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest]]\\n            [dao.test-slow :as slow]\\n            [yin.vm.ucf.stage-e-scenarios :as sc]))\\n\\n\\n(defn- run-all\\n  [scenarios]\\n  (doseq [s scenarios]\\n    (sc/run-in-process s)))\\n\\n\\n(deftest fork-per-host-test\\n  (run-all [sc/fork-row]))\\n\\n\\n(deftest ^:slow row-7-kills-around-completion-test\\n  (slow/guard\\n    \\\"row-7-kills-around-completion-test\\\"\\n    (fn []\\n      (run-all (map sc/row7 sc/row7-cuts)))))\\n\\n\\n(deftest row-7-failure-lower-and-lost-authority-test\\n  (run-all [sc/row7-failure-lower sc/row7-lost-authority]))\\n\\n\\n(deftest ^:slow row-4-kills-around-result-delivery-test\\n  (slow/guard\\n    \\\"row-4-kills-around-result-delivery-test\\\"\\n    (fn []\\n      (run-all (map sc/row4 sc/row4-cuts)))))\\n\\n\\n(deftest row-3-reclaim-test\\n  (run-all (map sc/row3 sc/row3-variants)))\\n\\n\\n(deftest row-5-replay-divergence-test\\n  (run-all (map sc/row5 sc/row5-variants)))\\n\\n\\n(deftest ^:slow row-2-export-phases-test\\n  (slow/guard\\n    \\\"row-2-export-phases-test\\\"\\n    (fn []\\n      (run-all (map sc/row2 (concat sc/row2-pre-fence-cuts sc/row2-post-fence-cuts))))))\\n\\n\\n(deftest ^:slow row-2-carrier-failures-test\\n  (slow/guard\\n    \\\"row-2-carrier-failures-test\\\"\\n    (fn []\\n      (run-all (map sc/row2-carrier sc/row2-carriers)))))\\n\\n\\n(deftest row-1-candidates-and-encodings-test\\n  (run-all [sc/row1]))\\n\\n\\n(deftest ^:slow row-6-partition-test\\n  (slow/guard\\n    \\\"row-6-partition-test\\\"\\n    (fn []\\n      (run-all [sc/row6-request-partition sc/row6-consumer-partition sc/row6-lost-reply]))))\\n\\n\\n(deftest ^:slow clause-8-admission-order-test\\n  (slow/guard\\n    \\\"clause-8-admission-order-test\\\"\\n    (fn []\\n      (run-all (concat (map sc/clause8 sc/clause8-variants) [sc/clause8-closed])))))\\n\\n\\n(deftest ^:slow clause-3-sequence-and-regrant-test\\n  (slow/guard\\n    \\\"clause-3-sequence-and-regrant-test\\\"\\n    (fn []\\n      (run-all [sc/clause3-regrant sc/clause3-carried]))))\\n\\n\\n(deftest ^:slow inbox-and-journal-cuts-test\\n  (slow/guard\\n    \\\"inbox-and-journal-cuts-test\\\"\\n    (fn []\\n      (run-all (concat (map #(sc/journal-row {:cut %}) sc/journal-cuts)\\n                       (map #(sc/journal-row {:fail %}) sc/uncertain-retentions))))))\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/1793600000000-engineer-module-pins-r2c.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:33:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_15\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1370,1418p' src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc; cat test/yin/vm/linker/layering_test.clj; cat test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_checkpoint_fixtures.cljc; rg -n 'fixture|\\\\\\\\.txt|mint' test/yin/vm/ucf/stage_e* test/yin/vm/ucf/*ledger*; sed -n '390,420p' test/yin/vm/semantic/safepoint_harness_test.cljc; sed -n '1350,1435p' test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"                    (item :simple arg pos))\\n        :else (item :float ai pos)))))\\n\\n\\n;; ==========================================================================\\n;; Decode, part 2: the closed Jing profile over generic items\\n;; ==========================================================================\\n\\n(declare item->value)\\n\\n\\n(defn- int-item\\n  \\\"The host big integer of an integer item (a bignum too when allowed),\\n   or nil.\\\"\\n  [bs x allow-bignum?]\\n  (case (:kind x)\\n    (:uint :nint) (:value x)\\n    :tag (let [[tag _] (:value x)]\\n           (when (and allow-bignum? (#{2 3} tag))\\n             (big (item->value bs x))))\\n    nil))\\n\\n\\n(defn- check-members\\n  \\\"Refuse duplicate raw encodings among items (dup-class), then\\n   portable-equality collapses among their values.\\\"\\n  [bs items values dup-class]\\n  (let [raws (map #(span-key bs (:start %) (:end %)) items)]\\n    (when (< (count (set raws)) (count items))\\n      (refuse dup-class)))\\n  (when (collapse? values)\\n    (refuse :equality-collapse)))\\n\\n\\n(defn- built\\n  \\\"coll, unless building it merged members the portable equality keeps\\n   apart (host identifier equality on ClojureScript compares the joined\\n   name): losing an entry is never acceptable.\\\"\\n  [coll expected]\\n  (when (< (count coll) expected)\\n    (refuse :host-collapse \\\"the host collection merged distinct members\\\"))\\n  coll)\\n\\n\\n(defn- pair-items\\n  \\\"The two items of a definite-or-indefinite two-element array item, or\\n   nil for any other shape.\\\"\\n  [p]\\n  (when (and (= :array (:kind p)) (= 2 (count (:value p))))\\n(ns yin.vm.linker.layering-test\\n  \\\"The linker's layering rule (collab design admission-in-linker r2,\\n   section 1): linker semantics is what a plain Clojure consumer needs,\\n   and the REPL is a consumer of it, never the reverse.  No namespace\\n   under src/cljc/yin/vm, src/cljc/yang or src/clj/dao requires a\\n   `yin.repl` namespace.  This gate reads the `ns` form of every source\\n   file there (tools.reader, reader conditionals preserved, so every\\n   branch is read, whether inside a clause or around whole clauses) and\\n   fails on any `yin.repl` or `yin.repl.*` symbol in a `:require`,\\n   `:require-macros` or `:use` clause, on any file it cannot read, on\\n   any file whose first form is not `ns` (empty files included), and on\\n   a root that is missing or holds no source file.  Docstrings and datum\\n   vocabulary such as `:yin.repl/root` are not requires and do not\\n   count.  JVM only: it reads source files.\\\"\\n  (:require [clojure.java.io :as io]\\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\\n            [clojure.tools.reader :as reader]\\n            [clojure.tools.reader.reader-types :as rt]))\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private roots\\n  [\\\"src/cljc/yin/vm\\\" \\\"src/cljc/yang\\\" \\\"src/clj/dao\\\"])\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private require-clauses\\n  #{:require :require-macros :use})\\n\\n\\n(defn- repl-ns?\\n  [x]\\n  (and (symbol? x)\\n       (let [s (str x)]\\n         (or (= \\\"yin.repl\\\" s) (.startsWith s \\\"yin.repl.\\\")))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- symbols-in\\n  [form]\\n  (cond\\n    (reader-conditional? form) (symbols-in (:form form))\\n    (symbol? form) [form]\\n    (coll? form) (mapcat symbols-in form)\\n    :else nil))\\n\\n\\n(defn- clauses\\n  \\\"The `ns` body elements with every reader conditional opened: each\\n   branch of a `#?` is one element, each branch of a `#?@` a sequence\\n   of elements, recursively, whatever the host.\\\"\\n  [body]\\n  (mapcat (fn [x]\\n            (if (reader-conditional? x)\\n              (let [branches (take-nth 2 (rest (:form x)))]\\n                (clauses (if (:splicing? x) (apply concat branches) branches)))\\n              [x]))\\n          body))\\n\\n\\n(defn repl-requires\\n  \\\"The `yin.repl` namespaces the `ns` form of `text` requires, as a\\n   sorted vector; `[:unreadable message]` when its first form cannot be\\n   read; `[:no-ns-form]` when its first form is not an `ns` form, which\\n   includes an empty file (every source file under `roots` is a\\n   namespace).\\\"\\n  [text]\\n  (try\\n    (binding [reader/*default-data-reader-fn* (fn [_ v] v)\\n              *ns* (create-ns 'yin.vm.linker.layering-reader)]\\n      (let [eof (Object.)\\n            form (reader/read {:read-cond :preserve, :eof eof}\\n                              (rt/indexing-push-back-reader text))]\\n        (if (and (seq? form) (= 'ns (first form)))\\n          (->> (clauses (rest form))\\n               (filter #(and (seq? %) (contains? require-clauses (first %))))\\n               (mapcat symbols-in)\\n               (filter repl-ns?)\\n               distinct\\n               sort\\n               vec)\\n          [:no-ns-form])))\\n    (catch Exception e\\n      [:unreadable (ex-message e)])))\\n\\n\\n(defn- source-files\\n  ([] (mapcat source-files roots))\\n  ([root]\\n   (->> (file-seq (io/file root))\\n        (filter #(.isFile ^java.io.File %))\\n        (map #(.getPath ^java.io.File %))\\n        (filter #(re-find #\\\"\\\\.clj[csd]?$\\\" %))\\n        sort)))\\n\\n\\n(defn violations\\n  \\\"file -> the `yin.repl` namespaces it requires, for every file under\\n   `roots` that requires one.\\\"\\n  []\\n  (into (sorted-map)\\n        (keep (fn [path]\\n                (let [found (repl-requires (slurp path))]\\n                  (when (seq found) [path found]))))\\n        (source-files)))\\n\\n\\n(deftest detector-sees-every-branch-test\\n  (testing \\\"a require in any reader-conditional branch is found\\\"\\n    (is (= '[yin.repl yin.repl.link]\\n           (repl-requires\\n             (str \\\"(ns a.b (:require [dao.stream :as s]\\\"\\n                  \\\" #?(:cljd [yin.repl.link :as l] :clj [x.y :as y])\\\"\\n                  \\\" #?@(:cljs [[yin.repl :as r]])))\\\")))))\\n  (testing \\\"#? wrapping a whole clause is read\\\"\\n    (is (= '[yin.repl.store]\\n           (repl-requires\\n             \\\"(ns a.b #?(:clj (:require [yin.repl.store :as store])))\\\"))))\\n  (testing \\\"#?@ wrapping whole clauses is read\\\"\\n    (is (= '[yin.repl yin.repl.link]\\n           (repl-requires\\n             (str \\\"(ns a.b #?@(:clj [(:require [dao.stream :as s])\\\"\\n                  \\\" (:use [yin.repl.link])]\\\"\\n                  \\\" :cljs [(:require-macros [yin.repl :as r])]))\\\")))))\\n  (testing \\\"a violation only in an inactive host branch is found\\\"\\n    (is (= '[yin.repl.store]\\n           (repl-requires\\n             (str \\\"(ns a.b #?(:clj (:require [dao.stream :as s])\\\"\\n                  \\\" :cljd (:require [yin.repl.store :as store])))\\\"))))\\n    (is (= '[yin.repl]\\n           (repl-requires\\n             (str \\\"(ns a.b #?(:cljs (:require [dao.stream :as s])\\\"\\n                  \\\" :default #?@(:clj [] :cljd [(:require [yin.repl])])))\\\")))))\\n  (testing \\\"a clean namespace with whole-clause conditionals stays clean\\\"\\n    (is (= []\\n           (repl-requires\\n             (str \\\"(ns a.b #?(:clj (:require [dao.stream :as s])\\\"\\n                  \\\" :cljd (:require [yin.vm.linker :as l]))\\\"\\n                  \\\" #?@(:clj [(:import (java.io File))]\\\"\\n                  \\\" :cljs [(:require [yin.repl-like :as x])]))\\\")))))\\n  (testing \\\"a file whose first form is not ns is an inspection failure\\\"\\n    (is (= :no-ns-form (first (repl-requires \\\"(def x 1) (ns a.b)\\\"))))\\n    (is (= :no-ns-form (first (repl-requires \\\"\\\"))))\\n    (is (= :no-ns-form (first (repl-requires \\\";; only a comment\\\\n\\\")))))\\n  (testing \\\"datum vocabulary and docstrings are not requires\\\"\\n    (is (= []\\n           (repl-requires\\n             (str \\\"(ns a.b \\\\\\\"yin.repl.link\\\\\\\" (:require [dao.stream :as s]))\\\"\\n                  \\\" (def k :yin.repl/root)\\\"))))))\\n\\n\\n(deftest every-root-is-inspected-test\\n  (doseq [root roots]\\n    (testing (str root \\\" exists and holds source files\\\")\\n      (is (.isDirectory (io/file root)))\\n      (is (seq (source-files root))))))\\n\\n\\n(deftest linker-requires-no-repl-test\\n  (testing (str \\\"no namespace under \\\" roots \\\" requires yin.repl\\\")\\n    (is (= {} (violations)))))\\n(ns yin.vm.ucf.rows-checkpoint-fixtures\\n  \\\"The shared canonical fixtures of the rows inspector (phase 7a, plan\\n   §3.3, §4 7a), pinned by their pack addresses, loaded on the JVM, Node\\n   and Dart.\\n\\n   The five accepted bases are packs rows/lift-task itself emitted under\\n   a custody header from real semantic machines\\n   (yin.vm.ucf.rows-support), the old checkpoint fixtures' five bases\\n   re-lifted. Nothing about a base is hand-built but its operation ids\\n   (`rows-support/with-op-id`). Every other fixture is a mutation of a\\n   named base: a task edit (decode, change the abstract task, `rows/emit`,\\n   so every row it touches is rehashed and the pack stays canonical), or a\\n   raw edit of the pack where the defect is the carrier's own (version,\\n   tag, row order, a row changed without rehash, a frame root). A\\n   mutation names the refusal it must draw, as a map the refusal must\\n   contain, computed from its base where a path depends on it.\\n\\n   The pins live in test/resources/yin/vm/ucf/rows-checkpoint-v3.txt, one\\n   block per fixture separated by a blank line: the name and the pack\\n   address of its bytes. Three anchors (`anchors`) also keep their full\\n   bytes as lowercase hex in lines of 64 digits, so the inspector reads\\n   bytes this build did not produce; every other fixture's bytes are built\\n   from its pack and checked against its pinned address. Regenerate the\\n   file from a JVM REPL with the string `render` returns, saved to `path`;\\n   the test proves on every host that the file equals `render`.\\n\\n   The test helpers below (`base`, `edit-task`, `edit-custody`, `enc`,\\n   the wait and child accessors) are what the authority's tests use to\\n   make their own packs from these bases.\\\"\\n  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\\n            [dao.jing.cbor-fixtures :as fx]\\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-support :as s]))\\n\\n\\n(def path\\n  \\\"The fixture file, relative to the repository root.\\\"\\n  \\\"test/resources/yin/vm/ucf/rows-checkpoint-v3.txt\\\")\\n\\n\\n(def max-exact rows/max-exact)\\n\\n(def occurrence s/occurrence)\\n(def predecessor s/predecessor)\\n(def origin s/origin)\\n(def arbitration s/arbitration)\\n(def op-id s/op-id)\\n\\n\\n;; =============================================================================\\n;; Accepted bases: real lifts\\n;; =============================================================================\\n\\n(defn- lifted\\n  [machine header]\\n  (let [w (s/lift machine header)]\\n    (when (contains? w :yin.k/status)\\n      (throw (ex-info \\\"A fixture base failed to lift\\\" w)))\\n    w))\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private base-packs\\n  (delay\\n    {\\\"first-park\\\" (lifted (s/parked-reader) (s/header 0 nil #{}))\\n     \\\"successor\\\" (lifted (s/with-op-id (s/parked-writer) :put (op-id 0)) (s/header 3 origin #{\\\"s0\\\"}))\\n     ;; a root waiting on an install whose child is blocked on a write\\n     ;; drawing id 4 from the root's sequence\\n     \\\"installs\\\" (lifted (assoc-in (s/parked-installer) [:installs 'host.mod :vm]\\n                                  (s/with-op-id (s/parked-writer) :put (op-id 4)))\\n                        (s/header 6 origin #{\\\"s0\\\"}))\\n     \\\"parked\\\" (lifted (s/parked-explicit) (s/header 1))\\n     \\\"halted-root\\\" (lifted (s/halted-machine) (s/header 0 origin #{}))}))\\n\\n\\n(def base-names [\\\"first-park\\\" \\\"successor\\\" \\\"installs\\\" \\\"parked\\\" \\\"halted-root\\\"])\\n\\n\\n(defn base\\n  \\\"The pack of accepted base n.\\\"\\n  [n]\\n  (get @base-packs n))\\n\\n\\n;; =============================================================================\\n;; Editing packs\\n;; =============================================================================\\n\\n(defn edit-task\\n  \\\"wire's root task through f, re-emitted: every changed row rehashed.\\\"\\n  [wire f]\\n  (rows/emit (f (rows/decode wire))))\\n\\n\\n(defn edit-custody\\n  \\\"wire with its root's custody slot through f.\\\"\\n  [wire f]\\n  (edit-task wire #(update-in % [:slots 16] f)))\\n\\n\\n(defn custody\\n  \\\"The custody slot of wire's root.\\\"\\n  [wire]\\n  (nth (:slots (rows/decode wire)) 16))\\n\\n\\n(defn waits\\n  [task]\\n  (nth (:slots task) 13))\\n\\n\\n(defn with-waits\\n  [task ws]\\n  (assoc-in task [:slots 13] (vec ws)))\\n\\n\\n(defn pending-of\\n  [wait]\\n  (second (:slots wait)))\\n\\n\\n(defn reason-of\\n  [wait]\\n  (first (:slots (pending-of wait))))\\n\\n\\n(defn wait-index\\n  \\\"The index of task's first wait whose pending reason is reason.\\\"\\n  [task reason]\\n  (or (first (keep-indexed #(when (= reason (reason-of %2)) %1) (waits task)))\\n      (throw (ex-info \\\"No wait of that reason\\\" {:reason reason}))))\\n\\n\\n(defn set-pending-slot\\n  \\\"wait with slot i of its pending row set to x.\\\"\\n  [wait i x]\\n  (assoc-in wait [:slots 1 :slots i] x))\\n\\n\\n(defn set-op-id\\n  [wait id]\\n  (set-pending-slot wait 3 id))\\n\\n\\n(defn update-put\\n  \\\"task with its first :put wait through f.\\\"\\n  [task f]\\n  (update-in task [:slots 13 (wait-index task :put)] f))\\n\\n\\n(defn install-index\\n  [task mn]\\n  (or (first (keep-indexed #(when (= mn (first (:slots %2))) %1) (nth (:slots task) 12)))\\n      (throw (ex-info \\\"No install of that name\\\" {:name mn}))))\\n\\n\\n(defn child\\n  [task mn]\\n  (nth (:slots (nth (nth (:slots task) 12) (install-index task mn))) 4))\\n\\n\\n(defn update-child\\n  [task mn f]\\n  (update-in task [:slots 12 (install-index task mn) :slots 4] f))\\n\\n\\n(defn segment-address\\n  \\\"The BLAKE3 segment address of host bytes.\\\"\\n  [bs]\\n  (keyword \\\"segment\\\" (str \\\"blake3-\\\" (jing/digest-bytes :blake3 bs))))\\n\\n\\n(defn enc\\n  \\\"A pack's canonical bytes and its pack address.\\\"\\n  [wire]\\n  (let [bs (cbor/encode wire)]\\n    {:address (segment-address bs) :bytes bs}))\\n\\n\\n;; =============================================================================\\n;; Mutations: the fixture is (f base)\\n;; =============================================================================\\n;;\\n;; :refusal is a function of the base to the map the inspector's refusal\\n;; must contain; an accepted variant names none.\\n\\n(defn- m\\n  ([n b f] {:name n :base b :f f})\\n  ([n b f refusal] {:name n :base b :f f :refusal refusal}))\\n\\n\\n(defn- custody-set\\n  [k x]\\n  #(edit-custody % (fn [c] (assoc c k x))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- custody-drop\\n  [k]\\n  #(edit-custody % (fn [c] (dissoc c k))))\\n\\n\\n(defn- undecodable\\n  [kind p]\\n  (constantly {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable :yin.k/kind kind :yin.k/path p}))\\n\\n\\n(defn- put-op\\n  \\\"The path of base wire's first :put wait's id, with tail appended.\\\"\\n  [wire & tail]\\n  (into [:frames (wait-index (rows/decode wire) :put) :op-id] tail))\\n\\n\\n(defn- child-put-op\\n  [wire & tail]\\n  (into [:installs 'host.mod :frames (wait-index (child (rows/decode wire) 'host.mod) :put) :op-id] tail))\\n\\n\\n(defn- edit-op-id\\n  [f]\\n  #(edit-task % (fn [t] (update-put t (fn [w] (set-op-id w (f (nth (:slots (pending-of w)) 3))))))))\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private origin-path [:custody :yin.k/origin])\\n\\n\\n(def ^:private mutations\\n  [;; accepted: variants of the successor\\n   ;; the same rows in another order: one root, another pack address\\n   (m \\\"variant-equal\\\" \\\"successor\\\" #(update % :yin.k/rows (comp vec reverse)))\\n   ;; another id counter: another root, the same custody and ids\\n   (m \\\"variant-other-root\\\" \\\"successor\\\" #(edit-task % (fn [t] (assoc-in t [:slots 4] 9))))\\n   (m \\\"variant-different-intent\\\" \\\"successor\\\"\\n      #(edit-task % (fn [t] (update-put t (fn [w] (set-pending-slot w 2 [:lit \\\"w\\\"]))))))\\n   (m \\\"variant-counter\\\" \\\"successor\\\" (custody-set :yin.k/next-op-seq 4))\\n   (m \\\"counter-at-bound\\\" \\\"successor\\\"\\n      #(-> %\\n           (edit-custody (fn [c] (assoc c :yin.k/next-op-seq max-exact)))\\n           (edit-task (fn [t] (update-put t (fn [w] (set-op-id w (op-id (dec max-exact)))))))))\\n   ;; bytes, gate and carrier\\n   (m \\\"hash-mismatch\\\" \\\"successor\\\" identity)\\n   (m \\\"non-canonical\\\" \\\"successor\\\" identity)\\n   (m \\\"version-float\\\" \\\"successor\\\" #(assoc % :yin.k/version (cbor/float64 3))\\n      (constantly {:yin.k/status :yin.k/profile-mismatch :yin.k/kind :version}))\\n   (m \\\"version-2\\\" \\\"successor\\\" #(assoc % :yin.k/version 2)\\n      (constantly {:yin.k/status :yin.k/profile-mismatch :yin.k/kind :version}))\\n   (m \\\"version-absent\\\" \\\"successor\\\" #(dissoc % :yin.k/version)\\n      (constantly {:yin.k/status :yin.k/profile-mismatch :yin.k/kind :version}))\\n   (m \\\"no-tag\\\" \\\"successor\\\" #(dissoc % :yin.k/handoff)\\n      (constantly {:yin.k/status :yin.k/profile-mismatch :yin.k/kind :version}))\\n   ;; a pack rooted at the successor's wait, not at a task\\n   (m \\\"frame-root\\\" \\\"successor\\\"\\n      #(rows/emit-numbered (nth (waits (rows/decode %)) 0) {})\\n      (undecodable :root [:yin.k/root]))\\n   ;; the store row's value changed, its id kept\\n   (m \\\"row-tampered\\\" \\\"successor\\\"\\n      (fn [w]\\n        (update w :yin.k/rows\\n                (fn [rs] (mapv #(if (= :store (second %)) (conj % 'tampered [:lit 1]) %) rs))))\\n      (constantly {:yin.k/status :yin.k/hash-mismatch :yin.k/kind :row}))\\n   (m \\\"bad-kind\\\" \\\"successor\\\" #(edit-task % (fn [t] (assoc-in t [:slots 2] :running)))\\n      (undecodable :kind [:kind]))\\n   (m \\\"root-role\\\" \\\"successor\\\" #(edit-task % (fn [t] (assoc-in t [:slots 3] :child)))\\n      (undecodable :role [:role]))\\n   ;; root custody\\n   (m \\\"missing-policy\\\" \\\"successor\\\" (custody-drop :yin.k/policy)\\n      (undecodable :missing-header [:custody :yin.k/policy]))\\n   (m \\\"missing-occurrence\\\" \\\"successor\\\" (custody-drop :yin.k/occurrence)\\n      (undecodable :missing-header [:custody :yin.k/occurrence]))\\n   (m \\\"missing-arbitration\\\" \\\"successor\\\" (custody-drop :yin.k/arbitration)\\n      (undecodable :missing-header [:custody :yin.k/arbitration]))\\n   (m \\\"missing-next-op-seq\\\" \\\"successor\\\" (custody-drop :yin.k/next-op-seq)\\n      (undecodable :missing-header [:custody :yin.k/next-op-seq]))\\n   ;; the draft's explicit fork spelling, not the ruled nil\\n   (m \\\"fork-policy\\\" \\\"successor\\\" (custody-set :yin.k/policy :yin.k/fork)\\n      (undecodable :policy [:custody :yin.k/policy]))\\n   (m \\\"nil-occurrence\\\" \\\"successor\\\" (custody-set :yin.k/occurrence nil)\\n      (undecodable :nil-occurrence [:custody :yin.k/occurrence]))\\n   (m \\\"occurrence-not-uuid\\\" \\\"successor\\\" (custody-set :yin.k/occurrence \\\"O\\\")\\n      (undecodable :malformed-occurrence [:custody :yin.k/occurrence]))\\n   (m \\\"origin-occurrence-not-uuid\\\" \\\"successor\\\" (custody-set :yin.k/origin (assoc origin :yin.k/occurrence \\\"O\\\"))\\n      (undecodable :malformed-origin origin-path))\\n   (m \\\"malformed-arbitration\\\" \\\"successor\\\" (custody-set :yin.k/arbitration (dissoc arbitration :dao.stream/descriptor))\\n      (undecodable :malformed-arbitration [:custody :yin.k/arbitration]))\\n   (m \\\"origin-is-self\\\" \\\"successor\\\" (custody-set :yin.k/origin (assoc origin :yin.k/occurrence occurrence))\\n      (undecodable :origin-is-self (conj origin-path :yin.k/occurrence)))\\n   (m \\\"malformed-origin\\\" \\\"successor\\\" (custody-set :yin.k/origin (dissoc origin :dao.lease/lease))\\n      (undecodable :malformed-origin origin-path))\\n   (m \\\"origin-nil-emitter\\\" \\\"successor\\\" (custody-set :yin.k/origin (assoc origin :yin.k/emitter nil))\\n      (undecodable :malformed-origin origin-path))\\n   (m \\\"counter-float\\\" \\\"successor\\\" (custody-set :yin.k/next-op-seq (cbor/float64 3))\\n      (undecodable :inexact [:custody :yin.k/next-op-seq]))\\n   (m \\\"counter-over-bound\\\" \\\"successor\\\" (custody-set :yin.k/next-op-seq (inc max-exact))\\n      (undecodable :inexact [:custody :yin.k/next-op-seq]))\\n   (m \\\"counter-negative\\\" \\\"successor\\\" (custody-set :yin.k/next-op-seq -1)\\n      (undecodable :inexact [:custody :yin.k/next-op-seq]))\\n   (m \\\"first-export-counter\\\" \\\"first-park\\\" (custody-set :yin.k/next-op-seq 1)\\n      (undecodable :first-export-counter [:custody :yin.k/next-op-seq]))\\n   (m \\\"halted-root-header\\\" \\\"halted-root\\\" (custody-set :yin.k/occurrence occurrence)\\n      (undecodable :halted-header [:custody :yin.k/occurrence]))\\n   (m \\\"halted-root-without-origin\\\" \\\"halted-root\\\" (custody-drop :yin.k/origin)\\n      (undecodable :missing-header origin-path))\\n   ;; lease, epoch and holder never enter a body (UCF 7.2.1)\\n   (m \\\"custody-epoch\\\" \\\"successor\\\" (custody-set :yin.k/epoch 0)\\n      (undecodable :custody-key [:custody :yin.k/epoch]))\\n   (m \\\"custody-lease\\\" \\\"successor\\\" (custody-set :dao.lease/lease \\\"lease-7\\\")\\n      (undecodable :custody-key [:custody :dao.lease/lease]))\\n   (m \\\"custody-not-map\\\" \\\"successor\\\" #(edit-custody % (constantly :yin.k/exclusive))\\n      (undecodable :malformed-custody [:custody]))\\n   ;; the child role and install completeness\\n   (m \\\"child-header\\\" \\\"installs\\\"\\n      #(edit-task % (fn [t] (update-child t 'host.mod (fn [c] (assoc-in c [:slots 16] {:yin.k/origin origin})))))\\n      (undecodable :child-header [:installs 'host.mod :custody]))\\n   (m \\\"install-without-entry\\\" \\\"installs\\\" #(edit-task % (fn [t] (assoc-in t [:slots 12] [])))\\n      (fn [w]\\n        {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable :yin.k/kind :incomplete-install\\n         :yin.k/path [:frames (wait-index (rows/decode w) :install)]}))\\n   ;; operation ids\\n   (m \\\"op-id-at-counter\\\" \\\"successor\\\" (edit-op-id #(assoc % :yin.k/seq 3))\\n      (fn [w] {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable :yin.k/kind :op-seq-range :yin.k/path (put-op w :yin.k/seq)}))\\n   (m \\