.cljc; sed -n '968,1005p' src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc; rg -n 'I-8|Q5|P2-1|R4|7.11|7.6.4|7.6.5' docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md docs/agents/known-gaps.md docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | tail -25\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"ERROR in (lift-pins-only-registry-answered-live-names) (rows.cljc:81)\\nUncaught exception, not in assertion.\\nexpected: nil\\n  actual: clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo: Row codec refused data\\n#:yin.k{:status :yin.k/profile-mismatch, :kind :version, :path [:yin.k/version]}\\n at yin.vm.ucf.rows$refuse_BANG_.invokeStatic (rows.cljc:81)\\n    yin.vm.ucf.rows$refuse_BANG_.invoke (rows.cljc:79)\\n    yin.vm.ucf.rows$decode_STAR_.invokeStatic (rows.cljc:849)\\n    yin.vm.ucf.rows$decode_STAR_.invoke (rows.cljc:839)\\n    yin.vm.ucf.rows$decode.invokeStatic (rows.cljc:971)\\n    yin.vm.ucf.rows$decode.invoke (rows.cljc:968)\\n    yin.vm.ucf.rows_test$pin_requires.invokeStatic (rows_test.cljc:1439)\\n    yin.vm.ucf.rows_test$pin_requires.invoke (rows_test.cljc:1437)\\n    yin.vm.ucf.rows_test$fn__21951.invokeStatic (rows_test.cljc:1464)\\n   every host runs the same seals. A test of cross-task forgery composes\\n   its tasks with distinct secrets.\\\"\\n  \\\"yin.vm.test-utils/capability-secret\\\")\\n\\n\\n(defn make-stream\\n  \\\"A `:make-stream` over the v2 ring buffer. A nil capacity is the VM's\\n   default, not an unbounded stream: v2 has no unbounded mode.\\\"\\n  [capacity]\\n  (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type,\\n                       ringbuffer/capacity-key (or capacity\\n                                                   vm/default-stream-capacity)}))\\n\\n\\n(defn new-stream\\n  \\\"Create one ring buffer handle or throw.\\\"\\n  ([] (new-stream default-capacity))\\n  ([capacity]\\n   (let [result (make-stream capacity)]\\n     (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:140:          (fail (str \\\"Unable to resolve symbol: \\\" name \\\" in this context\\\")\\n    (when-not (occurrence-origin? origin)\\n      (throw (ex-info \\\"Malformed source occurrence origin\\\"\\n                      {:rule :origin, :origin origin})))\\n    origin))\\n\\n\\n(defn loaded-code-floor\\n  \\\"The lowest entity id claimed by the segments in a `{segment-id image}`\\n   code map — each segment id minus its length — or 0 when none is loaded.\\n   A loader minting a fresh local segment id allocates below this floor\\n   (`semantic/load-ast` for projected AST batches, `semantic/load-vector`\\n   for canonical instruction vectors), so successive loads never collide\\n   with a live id.\\\"\\n  [code]\\n  (if (map? code)\\n    (reduce-kv (fn [floor seg image]\\n                 (if (and (integer? seg) (map? image))\\n                   (min floor (- seg (or (:length image) 0)))\\n                   floor))\\n               0\\n               code)\\n    0))\\n\\n\\n;; =============================================================================\\n;; Semantic bytecode: flat content-addressed rows\\n;; =============================================================================\\n;; docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md §2. One row `[id tag & slots]` per\\n;; distinct node; `id` is `(jing/segment-key [tag & slots])`.\\n\\n(def semantic-bytecode-grammar\\n  \\\"The Universal AST row-slot table (yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md §2.3):\\n   tag -> ordered `[field kind]` slots, rather than executable bytecode. Position `i` of a\\n   row body (after the tag) holds the map field named at `i`, so this one\\n   table drives both projection and reconstruction.\\\"\\n  {:literal [[:value :data]],\\n   :variable [[:name :sym]],\\n   :lambda [[:params :syms] [:body :node]],\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:714:**2026-10-16, I-8 (module-pins slice, partial; R4 only).** Lower now\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:723:Part B.1.3 versus step 8. I-8 is not complete.\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:10:> S7.11 lists the acceptance blockers that keep this warning standing until\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:36:(S7.6.1); S7.11 records the remaining definition-frame obligations.\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:41:(7.2.1, 7.4.3, 7.7.8, 7.9, 7.11.1). The amendment is published design:\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:66:and 7.6.1a (the source association and its completeness rule); 7.11 and\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:67:7.11.1 require the frame validator and cross-engine canonical equality\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:86:Every sentence in §7.2–§7.9 is a rule of the proposed protocol. §7.11 records\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:556:transition; see the revision log in S7.11. The de Bruijn images carry\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:598:`:yin.k/missing :yin.k/trees` and discovery is `:incomplete` (§7.6.5),\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:625:miss is `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming the address (§7.6.5); nothing from a\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1337:  publication is an acceptance blocker (S7.11).\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1498: :yin.k/discovery       :complete}                                     ; :complete | :incomplete | :blocked — computed, §7.6.5\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1512:`:yin.k/missing :yin.k/trees` and discovery is `:incomplete` (§7.6.5),\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1570:  retained requirement is `:yin.k/unsatisfied` (§7.6.5).\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1589:`:complete` from `:incomplete` from `:blocked` (§7.6.5); a fixed point that\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1695:### 7.6.4 Modules\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:1708:### 7.6.5 The satisfaction check\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2068:retention machine and