s not implemented | P1 |\\n| R4: carried install child bypasses receiver admission and carries sender evidence | fetch threat model §4.4 | VM Runtime | landed as module-pins commit 1 (origin/master ce76c846): explicit `:yin.k/admitted-modules` name/address gate before attach; lift never carries sender admission fields; a carried admission field refuses `:yin.k/undecodable :install-response`; the pin carrier is module-pins commit 2 | P1 |\\n| Composition fetch loop per-run lease and budget absent | fetch threat model §4.3; reserved `:lease` policy | composition | outside module-pins slice; no fetch loop added | P2 |\\n| Holder driver passes no admitted-modules map; install-child handoff through the driver refuses | Architect module-pins review P2-1 | VM Runtime | implemented in module-pins r2b (uncommitted): composition config retained and forwarded to lowering and fenced recovery; parked-installer driver regression covers absent and admitted config | P2 |\\n  contract; the receiver-side pin check remains required.\\n- **Q6, conservatism of the live-code rule.** `live-pcs` follows both\\n  successor edges of every branch and enters every reachable closure\\n  body, with no constant propagation. The harness's `(if false (fn []\\n  ghost) (next-of c))` case transports only because the lift happens at\\n  a safepoint **after** the branch (the resume pc is past it, so the\\n  dead arm is unreachable by edges); the same program lifted at a\\n  safepoint **before** the branch would refuse `ghost` although the arm\\n  can never run. Is \\\"reachable by control-flow edges, never by value\\\"\\n  the intended precision, accepting the false refusals it implies for\\n  constant-dead code?\\n- **Q7, host-class primitives behind a shadow.** `:host-state-primitive`\\n  refuses only when the name reaches the primitive step of the answering\\n  order; the same name bound in `E` or the active store lifts (codex\\n  round 2 confirmed). Intended, or should a host-class primitive name\\n  refuse regardless of shadowing?\\n- **Q8, preflight attachment cost.** `attaches?` validates and analyses\\n  every carried vector (and every install image) by attaching it into a\\n  throwaway receiver, and restore attaches it again. Codex found it pure\\n  and only duplicated CPU. Accept, or ask the kernel for a validate-only\\n  entry point?\\n- **Q9, Law 2 outside a fresh receiver.** The id counter is adopted as\\n  `max(local, carried)`; a receiver whose construction mints more ids\\n  than the carrier relifts to a different root (draft §9 already scopes\\n  the law to the fresh-receiver context). No harness case has a\\n  non-fresh receiver. Add one as a documented non-law, or leave it?\\n- **Q10, the `:running` wire phase's future.** If Q1 narrows the phase\\n  set, row 11 disappears from the matrix and the `:install` row's phase\\n  slot becomes a constant; if not, row 11 stays a synthetic case. Which?\\n\\n**Revision 5 (after 6c) adds the three questions the rulings left\\n(`collab/1792360000000-architect-6c-rulings.report.md`); they are\\nnumbered on their own, as 6c Q1-Q3, so the 6b numbering above stands.**\\n\\n- **6c Q1, the native-lane matrix scope (changes acceptance counts).\\n  ACCEPTED by the owner on 2026-10-13.** The de Bruijn lanes run the\\n  shared fragment: law 4 on 61 of the 89 cases, law 5 on 350 of the 534\\n  transfers, tail acceptance on rows 6 and 20 only.\\n\\n- **Authority grounding and wiring.** The arbitration `dao.space`, its\\n  transactor as grantor, the occurrence ledger with epochs, and the\\n  attribution resolver `dao.lease.md` requires, are composition duties; the\\n  first composition to ship UCF is `yin.repl.core`'s handoff demo, and\\n  its wiring becomes the worked example. A composition without a\\n  transactable space offers `:yin.k/fork` only.\\n- **Receiver module satisfaction and install admission (2026-10-16).**\\n  Architect verdict C requires registry bindings pinned by manifest address\\n  (§7.6.4/§7.6.5) and receiver re-discharge before attachment. The module-pin\\n  carrier uses `:yin.k/host-exports` in `requires` for used host export profile\\n  addresses (Architect Part B, ruled 2026-10-16). Implementation is pending:\\n  r2b stopped on conflicting empty-map emission instructions. Name presence\\n  does not establish equal-address satisfaction.\\n  Carried install admission (R4) is implemented by the lower's explicit\\n  `:yin.k/admitted-modules {name manifest-address}` option, default empty, and\\n  the lift never carries sender admission evidence; a carried admission field\\n  is refused as `:yin.k/undecodable :install-response`. The fetch loop remains\\n  composition work: fetch before the grant proposal (14.2.3 step 2), retry\\n  the same pack bytes, at most one require per missing module and two\\n\\nTesting yin.vm.linker.layering-test\\n\\nRan 33 tests containing 173 assertions.\\n0 failures, 0 errors.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/1793600000000-engineer-module-pins-r2c.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:73:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_36\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '430,458p' docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md; sed -n '2774,2790p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md; git diff -- test/yin/vm/engine_test.cljc test/yin/vm/linker/layering_test.clj\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"[T :task\\n   version          ; 3                       (gated first, §8)\\n   contract         ; {:yin.code/contract \\\"v4\\\" :yin.k/version 1}, the one profile map (§2)\\n   kind             ; :blocked | :parked | :halted\\n   role             ; :root | :child\\n   id-counter       ; N                       (UCF §7.6.3)\\n   free-env-cref    ; a :bindings row, the task's initial free environment (continuation §6.3)\\n   store-cref\\n   module-stores    ; crefs sorted by M\\n   parked-cref      ; :parked-table\\n   cursor-cells-cref       ; :cursor-cells census\\n   requires         ; plain: UCF §7.6.1's map plus :yin.k/trees (continuation §6.1)\\n   code             ; plain: {A canonical-vector …}, \\\"v4\\\" vectors verified to hash to their key\\n   installs         ; crefs to :install rows, sorted by module name\\n   frames           ; crefs to :wait rows, IN WAIT ORDER   (:blocked, :parked)\\n   parked-id        ; P or nil                              (:parked only)\\n   result           ; V or nil                              (:halted only)\\n   custody]         ; plain, see below\\n```\\n\\n(Root replaced 2026-10-11 by continuation §2.6: `free-env-cref` added,\\n`contract` is the one profile map, `code` holds `\\\"v4\\\"` canonical vectors,\\n`requires` gains `:yin.k/trees`.) No `layout` slot and no native image:\\nthose were the positional profiles' (v2 amendment §2, §4.1).\\n\\nKind rules are §7.2.1's: `:blocked` has nonempty frames and neither\\nparked-id nor result; `:parked` has frames (possibly empty), a parked-id\\nnaming a key of the parked table, no result; `:halted` has a result and\\nneither frames nor parked-id. Frames restore in carried order and are\\n- **Q5, answered C by the Architect threat model (2026-10-16);\\n  host-export carrier ruled in Architect Part B, implementation pending.** The ruling\\n  requires `requires {:yin.k/modules {name manifest-address-or-nil}}`,\\n  equal-address receiver re-discharge before attach, and equal export\\n  profile addresses for used exports of host-module nil pins through\\n  `:yin.k/host-exports {qualified-symbol profile-keyword}` in `requires`.\\n  The r2b implementation stopped on conflicting instructions about emitting\\n  empty pin maps (Part B.1.3 versus step 8). Until it lands, the implementation still\\n  has the following gap: free names are discharged at lift\\n  only (§7.1); the lower checks carried segments, trees, store census,\\n  closures and primitives, and a name a closure resolves through the\\n  registry is a composition prerequisite (§2.5). A receiver lacking that\\n  registry entry accepts the carrier and fails at run time\\n  (`Unable to resolve symbol`). This behavior is not the accepted final\\n  contract; the receiver-side pin check remains required.\\n- **Q6, conservatism of the live-code rule.** `live-pcs` follows both\\n  successor edges of every branch and enters every reachable closure\\ndiff --git a/test/yin/vm/engine_test.cljc b/test/yin/vm/engine_test.cljc\\nindex c9d3263b..832f15c0 100644\\n--- a/test/yin/vm/engine_test.cljc\\n+++ b/test/yin/vm/engine_test.cljc\\n@@ -877,3 +877,18 @@\\n                                  resume-fn)]\\n         (is (:halted? out))\\n         (is (= [:halt] (phase-seq sink)))))))\\n+\\n+\\n+(deftest unresolved-qualified-name-still-fails-without-fetch-or-park\\n+  (let [request (tu/new-stream 8)\\n+        response (tu/new-stream 8)\\n+        m (state {:link-request request :link-response response})\\n+        message (try\\n+                  (engine/resolve-var (:env m) (:store m) (:primitives m)\\n+                                      (:modules m) 'absent.mod/f)\\n+                  nil\\n+                  (catch #?(:clj Exception :cljs js/Error :cljd Object) e\\n+                    (ex-message e)))]\\n+    (is (= \\\"Unable to resolve symbol: absent.mod/f in this context\\\" message))\\n+    (is (empty? (tu/drain request)))\\n+    (is (empty? (tu/drain response)))))\\ndiff --git a/test/yin/vm/linker/layering_test.clj b/test/yin/vm/linker/layering_test.clj\\nindex ecc7b4c0..eb88a5df 100644\\n--- a/test/yin/vm/linker/layering_test.clj\\n+++ b/test/yin/vm/linker/layering_test.clj\\n@@ -156,3 +156,18 @@\\n (deftest linker-requires-no-repl-test\\n   (testing (str \\\"no namespace under \\\" roots \\\" requires yin.repl\\\")\\n     (is (= {} (violations)))))\\n+\\n+\\n+(deftest portable-evaluator-and-lower-have-no-fetch-or-lease-dependencies\\n+  (doseq [path (filter #(or (= % \\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc\\\")\\n+                           (= % \\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc\\\")\\n