                          {:modules registry :origin origin\n                                    :ancestry (conj (vec (:ancestry recv)) mn)\n                                    :capability-secret (when (fn? source) (source origin))})]\n    [(cond-> (dissoc child :yin.k/closes :yin.k/issued :yin.k/gate :yin.k/custody\n                     :yin.k/recovery-waits :yin.k/recovery-parked :yin.k/recovery-cell-ids)\n       fenced? (assoc :make-stream (:make-stream recv)))\n     (assoc recv :origins (inc n))]))\n\n\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:42:| Q5: receiver accepts registry dependencies by name only; Architect verdict C requires module identity pins and receiver re-discharge | fetch threat model §4.2, §6; Architect module-pins Part B | VM Runtime / Architect | host-export carrier ruled 2026-10-16: `:yin.k/host-exports` in `requires`; r2c resolves empties (both maps always present), but implementation stops on string-or-nil carrier values versus actual Jing keyword registry addresses (I-8); module pins not implemented | P1 |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2869:  (§7.6.4/§7.6.5) and receiver re-discharge before attachment. The module-pin\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:360:- **Linked registry entries do not travel.** The row table has no slot\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1700:   pc. Discharge runs at lift only; the lower does not re-discharge free\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1809:| dependencies | `check-dependencies!` | `requires` is a map whose `:yin.k/segments` equals the key set of `code` (`:requires`); every segment has a non-empty `:yin.k/trees` entry; every `store-of` of every `:closure` and `:env` row of **this task** (children excluded, each checked in its own stage pass) names one of this task's `:module-store` rows (§2.6), so a parent's or sibling's store of the same key cannot answer (codex F7, F8); every vector attaches in the receiving kernel under its A (`attaches?`: `module/attach-module` into