{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('test/yin/vm/ucf/stage_e_rows_test.cljc');s=p.read_text().replace('[clojure.test :refer [deftest]]','''[clojure.test :refer [deftest is]]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            [dao.jing.cbor-fixtures :as cfx]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-test :as pins]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-support :as support]''');s+='''\n\n(deftest module-pin-carrier-and-refusals-agree-on-every-host\n  (let [registry (pins/pin-registry)\n        profile (:yin.k/profile pins/pin-profile)\n        host-wire (support/lift (pins/pin-machine registry) nil)\n        linked (assoc-in registry [:modules 'host 'mod :address] :segment/sender)\n        linked-wire (support/lift (pins/pin-machine linked) nil)\n        hex #(cfx/bytes->hex (cbor/encode %))]\n    (is (= (hex host-wire) (hex (rows/emit (rows/decode host-wire)))))\n    (is (= {:yin.k/modules {'host.mod nil} :yin.k/host-exports {'host.mod/f profile}}\n           (select-keys (pins/pin-requires host-wire) [:yin.k/modules :yin.k/host-exports])))\n    (doseq [[wire recv expected]\n            [[linked-wire registry\n              {:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied :yin.k/kind :module-pin-mismatch\n               :yin.k/name 'host.mod :yin.k/pinned :segment/sender :yin.k/linked nil}]\n             [host-wire (assoc-in registry [:modules 'host 'mod :manifest :yin.module/primitives 'f] :profile/other)\n              {:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied :yin.k/kind :host-export-mismatch\n               :yin.k/name 'host.mod/f :yin.k/pinned profile :yin.k/held :profile/other}]\n             [host-wire (module/empty-registry)\n              {:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied :yin.k/discovery :complete\n               :yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {'host.mod nil} :yin.k/host-exports {'host.mod/f profile}}}]]]\n      (let [actual (pins/pin-lower-refusal recv wire)]\n        (is (= expected actual))\n        (is (= (hex expected) (hex actual)))))))\n''';p.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat > /tmp/module-pins-r2d-docs.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md');s=p.read_text();a=s.index('exports only. Implementation');b=s.index('\\\\n\\\\nKind rules',a);s=s[:a]+'''exports only. The module map is \"'`{module-symbol address-keyword-or-nil}`:\ncarry `(:address entry)` unchanged and compare with `=`. The earlier ruling'\"'s\nstring-or-nil wording was a typing slip; linked entries hold Jing segment\nkeywords. The host-export map is \"'`{qualified-symbol profile-keyword}`.\nBoth maps are validated during decode and dependency checking, including\nsymbol key cardinality. Malformed or absent maps refuse `:yin.k/undecodable\n:requires`. After custody, `check-modules!` checks every task before the first\nattach: terminal `:module-pin-mismatch` or `:host-export-mismatch` wins,\nthen one `:yin.k/unsatisfied` with `:yin.k/discovery :complete` collects\nmissing pins and unadmitted install children under `:yin.k/missing`.\n'\"'''+s[b:];p.write_text(s)\np=Path('docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md');s=p.read_text();a=s.index('- **Linked registry entries do not travel.**');b=s.index('- **Amended after 7',a);s=s[:a]+'''- **Linked registry entries do not travel.** Their binding facts travel in\n  \"'`requires`: `:yin.k/modules {name address-keyword-or-nil}` and\n  `:yin.k/host-exports {qualified-symbol profile-keyword}` for used host\n  exports only. Both maps are always present, including `{}`. The receiver'\"'s\n  registry stays as given and must satisfy exact address equality and each\n  used host export's profile equality before any stream attaches.\n'''+s[b:];s=s.replace('pc. Discharge runs at lift only; the lower does not re-discharge free\\\\n   names against the receiver (§7.2).','''pc. Registry answers record the entry's own address unchanged, and host\n   answers also record the used export's profile address. The lower\n   re-discharges these binding facts against the receiver (§7.2).''');s=s.replace('… :yin.k/trees …}\"'`;'\"','… :yin.k/trees … :yin.k/modules … :yin.k/host-exports …}\"'`;'\"');a=s.index('construction of the stages above. The lower does **not**');b=s.index(' The kinds ',a);s=s[:a]+'''construction of the stages above. \"'`check-modules!` checks bindings over the\nwhole tree after custody and before attachment: unequal held addresses or\nprofiles refuse terminally as `:module-pin-mismatch` or `:host-export-mismatch`;\nabsent bindings, absent exports and unadmitted install children are collected\nin one `:yin.k/unsatisfied` with `:yin.k/discovery :complete` and\n`:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules … :yin.k/host-exports …}` (only nonempty keys).\nThe receiver'\"'s registry is kept as given.'''+s[b:];s=s.replace('  :yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {name carried-address}}}', '  :yin.k/discovery :complete\\\\n  :yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {name carried-address}}}');a=s.index('- **Q5, answered C');b=s.index('- **Q6,',a);s=s[:a]+'''- **Q5, closed as C (2026-10-16, module-pins I-8).** Both pin maps\n  always travel in \"'`requires`; the lower checks exact entry address keywords\n  (or nil for hosts), and profile keywords for used host exports, before attach.\n  Missing keys are `:yin.k/undecodable :requires`. Terminal skew precedes\n  exhaustive missing discovery, including receiver admission for install\n  children. Fetch and the per-run lease remain composition work, outside this\n  slice; the pure lower performs neither.\n'\"'''+s[b:];needle='| custody | \"'`check-custody!`'\"';idx=s.index('\\\\n\\\\n**Amended 2026-10-16 (module-pins, R4).**');s=s[:idx]+'''\\\\n| modules | \"'`check-modules!` | Whole-tree module address and used host-export profile equality; carried install children require receiver admission; after custody, before attach | `:yin.k/unsatisfied :module-pin-mismatch`, `:host-export-mismatch`, or collected missing with `:yin.k/discovery :complete` |'\"'''+s[idx:];p.write_text(s)\np=Path('docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md');s=p.read_text();idx=s.index('\\\\n### 7.6.5');s=s[:idx]+'''\\\\nThe row carrier implements this as required \"'`:yin.k/modules\n{module-symbol address-keyword-or-nil}` and `:yin.k/host-exports\n{qualified-symbol profile-keyword}` maps in `requires`, both `{}` when empty.\nEntry addresses travel unchanged. Host entries pin nil and each used export'\"'s\nprofile address; unused exports impose no requirement. Before attachment,\nterminal module/profile skew precedes one complete collected missing outcome,\nincluding unadmitted carried install children.\\\\n'''+s[idx:];s=s.replace(':yin.k/modules        {my.mod …}',':yin.k/modules        {my.mod …}\\\\n                   :yin.k/host-exports   {host.mod/f <expected profile>}');a=s.index('  carrier uses \"'`:yin.k/host-exports`'\"');b=s.index('  Carried install admission',a);s=s[:a]+'''  carrier implements both required pin maps, including \"'`{}` when empty,\n  with module entry address keywords carried unchanged (I-8). The lower\n  checks exact module and used export profile equality before attach;\n  terminal mismatches precede complete collected missing discovery.\n'\"'''+s[b:];p.write_text(s)\np=Path('docs/agents/known-gaps.md');s=p.read_text();lines=s.splitlines();lines=[('| Closed 2026-10-16: Q5 receiver module and used host-export pins | Architect module-pins Part B; I-8 | VM Runtime | implemented in uncommitted module-pins commit 2: exact keyword addresses and profile equality, complete collected refusal before attach | P1 |' if x.startswith('| Q5:') else '| Closed 2026-10-16: holder driver forwards admitted-modules | Architect module-pins review P2-1 | VM Runtime | config forwarded to lowering and fenced recovery; parked-installer regression covers absent and admitted config | P2 |' if x.startswith('| Holder driver passes') else x) for x in lines];p.write_text('\\\\n'.join(lines)+'\\\\n')\nPY\npython3 /tmp/module-pins-r2d-docs.py\nrg -n '\"'^FAIL|''^ERROR|actual:'\"' /tmp/module-pins-r2d-rows3.log | head -55\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
